{"parentUuid":"b468680b-3f67-40b4-b601-e389b6127922","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs894hMGi9RUnG2LtUQS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":372273,"output_tokens":1160,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":112},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1160,"cache_read_input_tokens":372273,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7619,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cfs894K2iiDGeu6bGvUCp","type":"assistant","uuid":"0f238d64-c1f4-415c-b8f4-a88be7003a64","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:18:53.300Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"0f238d64-c1f4-415c-b8f4-a88be7003a64","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs894hMGi9RUnG2LtUQS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committed locally as `f781602`, not pushed. Your last three messages are all handled:\n\n- **Figures:** the stick figures are gone. There are now three chunky figures in the style of your references, with big heads, faces, eyes, brows, smiles and blush, and hard hats.\n  - Lead architect: yellow hat, glasses, blue shirt with rolled sleeves, jeans, rolled plans.\n  - Architect: white hat, long hair, black blazer over a cream blouse, ruler and pencil.\n  - Site engineer: orange hat, hi-vis vest with reflective stripes, survey staff.\n- **Walking:** proper walk cycle now. Knees bend, feet don't slide, arms swing opposite the legs, the head bobs a little behind the step, and they speed up and slow down instead of snapping.\n- **Opening lines:** no more random lines. The engineer stakes the corners and walks the boundary, one architect marks the setbacks, the other draws the zone dividers. Then the three of them huddle at the front of the plot until the schemes arrive.\n- **Critics:** specialists walk on in their colour carrying clipboards. Each one stands at the room they're talking about and takes notes. Then they say their finding in a speech bubble, which is the engine's actual remark. A free team member walks over, takes the handed note and answers (\"Noted.\", \"Good catch. We'll revise it.\"), the critic leaves, and the team member points at the room. If the whole team is busy drawing, the critic talks to another critic instead. At most three bubbles show at once.\n- **Drone camera:** it moves in close on the floor being drawn, follows the rooms being worked on, moves to the other floor when the work does, and pulls back out between phases.\n- **Bar vs figures:** the slowdown came from slow frames. Time per frame was capped, so a busy page put the figures in slow motion, and they only caught up at the end. They now run on real time and speed up as the engine gets near the end. On the result they sprint to finish, critics vanish where they stand, nobody walks off screen, and the bar only fills once the board has settled. The end sequence is capped at 2.6 s, shorter than before.\n- **Review screen:** one drawing area plus one side panel showing:\n  - the score\n  - cost, area, Vastu and findings\n  - the committee\n  - the brief, collapsed\n\n  The left rail and bottom strip are gone. Drawings are grouped into six sets instead of 12 tabs, and the top bar has six views: Drawings, 3D, Vastu, Cost, Interior, Report. The 3D tab is now a real model you can drag to orbit and scroll to zoom.\n- **Star field:** I hid it on the run and review screens. It was showing through the drawing as a dot cluster. It still plays on the brief screen.\n\nI checked all of this with screenshots and found no console errors. But the preview browser here only moves the animation forward when I take a screenshot, so I stepped through the frames by hand. Watch one run in your own browser to confirm the motion looks smooth at full speed.\n\n**Not done yet:** the airflow drawing redesign. It still uses the rainbow colours and the cramped header, and it's next."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":372273,"output_tokens":1160,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":112},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1160,"cache_read_input_tokens":372273,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_cr