{"parentUuid":"616c219a-a1d2-49ab-ae32-e21bd77d177b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfsDgMP948tTRgcWq4i3w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gy3QzfZgzUDnpXVC85vtLE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/f/Users/shrey/Desktop/Studiorabbit-V2\" && cat .claude/launch.json server.mjs | head -60; wc -c site/index.html tools/original-css/*.css tools/hero/* tools/loader/*; head -c 3000 HERO-VIDEO-PROMPTS.md","description":"Inspect the reference site's server, sizes and notes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1686,"cache_read_input_tokens":374586,"output_tokens":192,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1686,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":192,"cache_read_input_tokens":374586,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1686,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1686},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Gy3QzfZgzUDnpXVC85vtLE":{"command":"cd \"/f/Users/shrey/Desktop/Studiorabbit-V2\" && cat .claude/launch.json server.mjs | head -60; wc -c site/index.html tools/original-css/*.css tools/hero/* tools/loader/*; head -c 3000 HERO-VIDEO-PROMPTS.md","description":"Inspect the reference site's server, sizes and notes"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfsDgM4YhR5o6bGvBETtv","type":"assistant","uuid":"e219caa5-662e-41e5-ab0c-4d83f2129c32","timestamp":"2026-10-09T19:31:25.372Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"e219caa5-662e-41e5-ab0c-4d83f2129c32","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cde90b88-60f3-4a8e-aba6-b51e470ae5ea","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Gy3QzfZgzUDnpXVC85vtLE","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"version\": \"0.0.1\",\n  \"configurations\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"site\",\n      \"runtimeExecutable\": \"node\",\n      \"runtimeArgs\": [\"server.mjs\", \"8080\"],\n      \"port\": 8080\n    }\n  ]\n}\n// Local static server for ./site (zero dependencies).\n// Usage: node server.mjs [port]   -> http://localhost:8080\nimport http from 'node:http';\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nimport { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n\nconst ROOT = path.join(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), 'site');\nconst PORT = +process.argv[2] || 8080;\nconst TYPES = {\n  '.html': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', '.css': 'text/css', '.js': 'text/javascript', '.json': 'application/json',\n  '.webmanifest': 'application/manifest+json', '.svg': 'image/svg+xml', '.png': 'image/png', '.jpg': 'image/jpeg',\n  '.jpeg': 'image/jpeg', '.gif': 'image/gif', '.webp': 'image/webp', '.ico': 'image/x-icon', '.mp4': 'video/mp4',\n  '.woff': 'font/woff', '.woff2': 'font/woff2', '.txt': 'text/plain', '.xml': 'application/xml',\n  '.avif': 'image/avif', '.gltf': 'model/gltf+json', '.bin': 'application/octet-stream',\n};\n\nfunction resolve(urlPath) {\n  const p = path.normalize(decodeURIComponent(urlPath)).replace(/^(\\.\\.[/\\\\])+/, '');\n  const full = path.join(ROOT, p);\n  if (!full.startsWith(ROOT)) return null;\n  for (const c of [full, path.join(full, 'index.html'), full + '.html']) {\n    try { if (fs.statSync(c).isFile()) return c; } catch {}\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n\nhttp.createServer((req, res) => {\n  const urlPath = new URL(req.url, 'http://x').pathname;\n  let file = resolve(urlPath);\n  let status = 200;\n  if (!file) { file = path.join(ROOT, '404', 'index.html'); status = 404; }\n  const type = TYPES[path.extname(file).toLowerCase()] || 'application/octet-stream';\n  const size = fs.statSync(file).size;\n  const range = req.headers.range;\n  // Range support so videos can seek/scrub\n  if (range && status === 200) {\n    const [s, e] = range.replace('bytes=', '').split('-');\n    const start = +s, end = e ? +e : size - 1;\n    res.writeHead(206, { 'Content-Type': type, 'Content-Range': `bytes ${start}-${end}/${size}`, 'Accept-Ranges': 'bytes', 'Content-Length': end - start + 1 });\n    fs.createReadStream(file, { start, end }).pipe(res);\n    return;\n  }\n  res.writeHead(status, { 'Content-Type': type, 'Content-Length': size, 'Accept-Ranges': 'bytes', 'Cache-Control': 'no-cache' });\n  if (req.method === 'HEAD') return res.end();\n  fs.createReadStream(file).pipe(res);\n  if (status === 404) console.log('404', urlPath);\n}).listen(PORT, () => console.log(`Serving ${ROOT} at http://localhost:${PORT}`));\n236540 site/index.html\n  5202 tools/original-css/browser-message.css\n   464 tools/original-css/error.css\n172567 tools/original-css/global.css\n 56787 tools/original-css/landing.css\n 16374 tools/original-css/location.css\n  1713 tools/original-css/privacy-policy.css\n  6830 tools/hero/hero.css\n  6030 tools/hero/hero.js\n  1291 tools/loader/loader.css\n  3261 tools/loader/loader.js\n 28381 tools/loader/signature.png\n535440 total\n# Hero walkthrough video — Google Flow prompts\n\nOne continuous camera move through a dark, premium house, built from four 8-second clips.\nEach clip continues from the previous clip's last frame. The hero maps one clip to each scroll chapter:\n**01 Arrival → 02 Volume → 03 Ascent → 04 Horizon**.\n\n## Flow settings\n- **Model:** Veo 3.1 (Quality). **Aspect:** 16:9. Download at **1080p** (use Flow's upscale).\n- **Clip 1:** Text to Video. Make 2–4 takes and pick the one with the steadiest constant-speed glide and a dark centre in the first second, because the site title sits there.\n- **Clips 2–4:** Frames to Video, with the previous clip's **last frame as the start frame**, or Scenebuilder → **Extend**, which does the same. Leave the end frame empty. Only add one if a take drifts off-plan and you need to pull it back.\n- Paste the **Camera**, **Style** and **Avoid** blocks into every prompt **unchanged**. Repeating them word for word is what keeps the clips consistent.\n- Reject any take that has a cut, changes speed in its last second, or has furniture changing shape. Joins only feel seamless when speed and direction match at the boundary.\n- Audio doesn't matter; the site plays the video muted.\n\n---\n\n## Blocks to paste into every prompt\n\n**Camera:** One continuous gimbal-stabilised shot at eye level (about 1.5 m), moving at a slow, perfectly constant speed: no acceleration, no shake, no cuts, no zoom, no fades. Vertical lines stay vertical.\n\n**Style:** Ultra-premium architectural cinematography, photoreal, large-format cinema camera, 24mm spherical lens, 24fps with natural motion blur. Monochrome near-black palette of charcoal stone, honed black basalt, black-stained oak, smoked glass and brushed dark bronze. Lit only by warm 2700K concealed linear lighting and soft blue-hour light from outside, with creamy warm highlights and deep, clean shadows. Glossy surfaces carry long, soft reflections. Calm, silent, expensive. Fine film grain, gentle contrast, no saturated colours.\n\n**Avoid:** No people, animals, text, logos, signage, screens or TVs. No lens flares, flicker, morphing or melting furniture, sudden lighting changes or fisheye distortion.\n\n---\n\n## Clip 1 — Arrival (Text to Video)\n\nA single continuous 8-second shot. The camera glides slowly forward down a long, perfectly symmetrical entrance gallery inside a dark modern luxury house: tall walls of textured charcoal stone, a polished black basalt floor reflecting thin lines of warm light set into the ceiling and along the base of the walls. At the far end, a tall open pivot door of dark bronze frames a glimpse of a double-height living room glowing softly with warm light, with blue-hour sky beyond. The centre of the frame stays deep and dark at the start; as the camera advances, the doorway grows larger and the warm glow beyond becomes clearer. The shot ends mid-glide, just before the threshold, with the camera still moving forward.\n*(+ Camera, Style, Avoid)*\n\n## Clip 2 — Volume (start\nShell cwd was reset to F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"a22d0ec8-e283-42e2-94fd-c9e15906ee96","timestamp":"2026-10-09T19:31:28.040Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e219caa5-662e-41e5-ab0c-4d83f2129c32","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
