{"parentUuid":"6342118c-8530-4696-a171-b530a9e0f8d9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfsFYRrXsDAyDUWWG9iqV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016AaPCSgMBijTs4tCqhTouK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd ~/.claude/skills/impeccable/reference && sed -n 251,330p document.md","description":"Read the design.json sidecar schema"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4393,"cache_read_input_tokens":552676,"output_tokens":263,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":152},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4393,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":263,"cache_read_input_tokens":552676,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4393,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4393},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016AaPCSgMBijTs4tCqhTouK":{"command":"cd ~/.claude/skills/impeccable/reference && sed -n 251,330p document.md","description":"Read the design.json sidecar schema"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfsFYRWxFrQ22VPzeue7g","attributionSkill":"impeccable","type":"assistant","uuid":"c8cbfbaa-0d9d-42a5-ada1-35246dfd7cd3","timestamp":"2026-10-09T19:55:52.455Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"c8cbfbaa-0d9d-42a5-ada1-35246dfd7cd3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cde90b88-60f3-4a8e-aba6-b51e470ae5ea","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016AaPCSgMBijTs4tCqhTouK","type":"tool_result","content":"### Step 4b: Write .impeccable/design.json sidecar (extensions only)\n\nThe frontmatter owns token primitives (colors, typography, rounded, spacing, components). The sidecar at `.impeccable/design.json` carries **what Stitch's schema can't hold**: tonal ramps per color, shadow/elevation tokens, motion tokens, breakpoints, full component HTML/CSS snippets (the panel renders these into a shadow DOM), and narrative (north star, rules, do's/don'ts). It extends the frontmatter, it doesn't duplicate it.\n\nRegenerate the sidecar whenever you regenerate root `DESIGN.md`. If the user only asks to refresh the sidecar (e.g., from the live panel's stale-hint), preserve `DESIGN.md` and write only `.impeccable/design.json`.\n\n#### Schema\n\n```json\n{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 2,\n  \"generatedAt\": \"ISO-8601 string\",\n  \"title\": \"Design System: [Project Title]\",\n  \"extensions\": {\n    \"colorMeta\": {\n      \"primary\":        { \"role\": \"primary\",  \"displayName\": \"Editorial Magenta\", \"canonical\": \"oklch(60% 0.25 350)\", \"tonalRamp\": [\"...\", \"...\", \"...\"] },\n      \"cool-paper\": { \"role\": \"neutral\",  \"displayName\": \"Cool Paper\",    \"canonical\": \"oklch(96% 0.005 230)\", \"tonalRamp\": [\"...\", \"...\", \"...\"] }\n    },\n    \"typographyMeta\": {\n      \"display\": { \"displayName\": \"Display\", \"purpose\": \"Hero headlines only.\" }\n    },\n    \"shadows\": [\n      { \"name\": \"ambient-low\", \"value\": \"0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.12)\", \"purpose\": \"Diffuse hover glow under accent elements.\" }\n    ],\n    \"motion\": [\n      { \"name\": \"ease-standard\", \"value\": \"cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1)\", \"purpose\": \"Default easing for state transitions.\" }\n    ],\n    \"breakpoints\": [\n      { \"name\": \"sm\", \"value\": \"640px\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"components\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Primary Button\",\n      \"kind\": \"button | input | nav | chip | card | custom\",\n      \"refersTo\": \"button-primary\",\n      \"description\": \"One-line what and when.\",\n      \"html\": \"<button class=\\\"ds-btn-primary\\\">SAVE CHANGES</button>\",\n      \"css\": \".ds-btn-primary { background: #191c1d; color: #fff; padding: 16px 48px; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; font-weight: 500; border: none; border-radius: 0; transition: background 0.2s, transform 0.2s; } .ds-btn-primary:hover { background: oklch(60% 0.25 350); transform: translateY(-2px); }\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": {\n    \"northStar\": \"The Editorial Sanctuary\",\n    \"overview\": \"2-3 paragraphs of the philosophy, pulled from DESIGN.md Overview section.\",\n    \"keyCharacteristics\": [\"...\", \"...\"],\n    \"rules\": [{ \"name\": \"The One Voice Rule\", \"body\": \"...\", \"section\": \"colors|typography|elevation\" }],\n    \"dos\":   [\"Do use ...\"],\n    \"donts\": [\"Don't use ...\"]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n**What changed from schemaVersion 1.** The old sidecar carried token primitive arrays (`tokens.colors[]`, `tokens.typography[]`, etc.). Those values now live in the frontmatter. The sidecar only carries metadata that can't live in the frontmatter (tonal ramps, canonical OKLCH when the hex is an approximation, display names, role hints), keyed by the frontmatter token name (`colorMeta.<token-name>`, `typographyMeta.<token-name>`). Components still carry full HTML/CSS because Stitch's 8-prop set can't hold them.\n\n#### Component translation rules\n\nThe `html` and `css` fields must be **self-contained, drop-in snippets** that render correctly when injected into a shadow DOM. The panel applies them directly: no post-processing, no framework runtime.\n\n1. **Tailwind expansion.** If the source uses Tailwind (className=\"bg-primary text-white rounded-lg px-6 py-3\"), expand every utility to literal CSS properties in the `css` string. Do **not** reference Tailwind classes; do **not** assume a Tailwind CSS bundle is loaded. Each component is self-contained.\n2. **Token resolution.** If the project exposes tokens as CSS custom properties on `:root` (e.g. `--color-primary`, `--radius-md`), reference them via `var(--color-primary)`; they inherit through the shadow DOM and stay live-bound. If tokens live only in JS theme objects (styled-components, CSS-in-JS), resolve to literal values at generation time.\n3. **Icons.** Inline as SVG. Do not reference Lucide/Heroicons packages, icon fonts, or `<img src=\"...\">`. A typical icon is 16-24px; copy the SVG path data directly.\n4. **States.** Include `:hover`, `:focus-visible`, and (if meaningful) `:active` rules inline. A static default-only snapshot makes the panel feel dead. Hover + focus rules in the CSS make it feel alive.\n5. **Reset bloat.** Extract only the component's *distinctive* CSS (background, color, padding, border-radius, typography, transition). Skip universal resets (`box-sizing: border-box`, `line-height: inherit`, `-webkit-font-smoothing`). The panel already has a neutral canvas; don't re-ship resets.\n6. **Scoped class names.** Prefix every class with `ds-` (e.g. `ds-btn-primary`, `ds-input-search`) so component CSS doesn't collide with other components' CSS in the same shadow DOM.\n\n#### What to include\n\nAim for a tight set of **5-10 components** that best represent the visual system:\n\n- **Canonical primitives (always include if the project has them):** button (each variant as a separate component entry), input/text field, navigation, chip/tag, card.\n- **Signature components (include if distinctive):** the recurring custom patterns that actually define the implemented system.\n- **Skip the rest.** Utility components, form building blocks, wrapper layouts: not worth documenting unless visually distinctive.\n\nIf the project has **no component library yet** (bare landing page, new project), synthesize canonical primitives from the tokens using best-practice defaults consistent with the DESIGN.md's rules. Every `.impeccable/design.json` has *something* to render, even on day zero.\n\n#### Tonal ramps\n\nFor each color token, generate an 8-step `tonalRamp` array: dark to light, same hue and chroma, stepped lightness from ~15% to ~95%. The panel renders this as a strip under the swatch. If the project already defines a tonal scale (Material `surface-container-low` family, Tailwind-style `blue-50..blue-900`), use those values. Otherwise synthesize in OKLCH.\n\n#### Narrative mapping\nShell cwd was reset to F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"72b8e8f7-477f-460b-90df-a14af7386e69","timestamp":"2026-10-09T19:55:52.880Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c8cbfbaa-0d9d-42a5-ada1-35246dfd7cd3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"72b8e8f7-477f-460b-90df-a14af7386e69","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14817058 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a5a224f5-74ed-4759-bd76-94250092f3ea","timestamp":"2026-10-09T19:55:52.923Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14817058 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"a5a224f5-74ed-4759-bd76-94250092f3ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfsFYkmaCj62bxYqB9rSX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01951G5VPtvsmEq7HTfyVDLM","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\DESIGN.md","content":"---\nname: Atri Arch Studio\ndescription: A studio of architects and thirteen specialists, in the Studio Rabbit world of warm black, cream and grain.\ncolors:\n  ink: \"#0b0a09\"\n  coal: \"#141312\"\n  soot: \"#1a1919\"\n  cream: \"#ede6dc\"\n  cream-2: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.74)\"\n  cream-3: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.5)\"\n  cream-4: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.3)\"\n  rule: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.1)\"\n  rule-2: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.2)\"\n  brick: \"#c4553f\"\n  stone: \"#a39c92\"\n  sand: \"#c9b497\"\n  pale-cream: \"#e8dcc6\"\ntypography:\n  display:\n    fontFamily: \"Archivo, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"\n    fontSize: \"clamp(46px, 6.2vw, 96px)\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: 0.92\n    letterSpacing: \"-0.025em\"\n    fontVariation: \"'wdth' 94\"\n  soft:\n    fontFamily: \"Archivo, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"\n    fontSize: \"clamp(26px, 2.9vw, 46px)\"\n    fontWeight: 300\n    lineHeight: 1.05\n    letterSpacing: \"-0.01em\"\n  headline:\n    fontFamily: \"Archivo, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"\n    fontSize: \"30px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: 1\n    letterSpacing: \"-0.01em\"\n  body:\n    fontFamily: \"Geist, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"\n    fontSize: \"15px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: 1.5\n  label:\n    fontFamily: \"Geist, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"\n    fontSize: \"11px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    letterSpacing: \"0.14em\"\nrounded:\n  pill: \"999px\"\n  panel: \"16px\"\n  frame: \"14px\"\n  cell: \"6px\"\nspacing:\n  gutter: \"clamp(16px, 3.2vw, 48px)\"\n  row: \"16px\"\n  group: \"clamp(40px, 6vh, 64px)\"\ncomponents:\n  button-primary:\n    backgroundColor: \"{colors.cream}\"\n    textColor: \"{colors.ink}\"\n    typography: \"{typography.label}\"\n    rounded: \"{rounded.pill}\"\n    height: \"56px\"\n    padding: \"0 30px\"\n  button-line:\n    backgroundColor: \"transparent\"\n    textColor: \"{colors.cream}\"\n    rounded: \"{rounded.pill}\"\n    height: \"40px\"\n    padding: \"0 20px\"\n  toggle-on:\n    backgroundColor: \"{colors.cream}\"\n    textColor: \"{colors.ink}\"\n    rounded: \"{rounded.pill}\"\n    padding: \"8px 15px\"\n  input-underline:\n    backgroundColor: \"transparent\"\n    textColor: \"{colors.cream}\"\n    padding: \"2px 0 4px\"\n---\n\n# Design System: Atri Arch Studio\n\n## Overview\n\n**Creative North Star: \"The Studio After Dark\"**\n\nThe studio runs in the Studio Rabbit world: a warm black room, cream type, the grain of film over everything, and nothing that glows. Content is set the way that site sets its chapters: what matters goes large, uppercase and tight in Archivo, the soft line beside it in Archivo italic, and everything you operate in quiet Geist. The brief is the project's title, so the first screen is the house being asked for, typeset and drawn to scale as you type.\n\nStructure comes from hairline rules, not boxes. There are no cards, no glass panels and no gradients standing in for depth. Colour is almost absent: cream at four strengths does the work, a few warm neutrals tell disciplines apart, and one brick red means something is wrong.\n\n**Key Characteristics:**\n- Warm black ground, cream type, animated film grain at 6%.\n- Archivo uppercase display with an italic soft line; Geist for UI and tracked uppercase labels.\n- Hairline rules and pill controls; cream-filled selection.\n- Brick red is the only signal colour.\n- One authored moment per screen: the self-drawing brief, the 3D studio at work, the drawing that carries into the review.\n\n## Colors\n\nA warm monochrome: black with a little brown in it, cream with a little paper in it.\n\n### Primary\n- **Cream** (#ede6dc): all primary text, the primary button, selected toggles and tabs, line work in drawings and the 3D board.\n\n### Neutral\n- **Ink** (#0b0a09): the ground everywhere, and the 3D board's clear colour.\n- **Coal** (#141312) and **Soot** (#1a1919): raised surfaces only: dialogs, toasts, speech bubbles, the drawing sheet.\n- **Cream at 74 / 50 / 30%**: secondary text, labels, faint captions. **Rules at 10 / 20%**: every divider and control outline.\n- **Stone** (#a39c92), **Sand** (#c9b497), **Pale cream** (#e8dcc6): discipline marks (analysis, structure and cost, judgement and Vastu), mandala quarters and the airflow ramp's upper end. They are tones, never fills of a region.\n\n### Tertiary\n- **Brick** (#c4553f): breaches, critical findings, low scores, a sealed room in the airflow diagram, the toast dot. Nothing decorative.\n\n### Named Rules\n**The One Signal Rule.** Brick red appears only where something fails. If a screen shows red, it is telling you about a problem.\n\n## Typography\n\n**Display Font:** Archivo (variable, width 94%), self-hosted.\n**Body Font:** Geist (variable), self-hosted. Both are taken from the Studio Rabbit site.\n\n### Hierarchy\n- **Display** (500, clamp(46px, 6.2vw, 96px), line-height 0.92, -0.025em, uppercase): the brief headline's hard lines, the run's stage word, the review score (84px).\n- **Soft** (Archivo italic 300, clamp(26px, 2.9vw, 46px)): the brief headline's soft lines, the run title, spoken narration in the 3D tab.\n- **Headline** (Archivo 500, 30px, uppercase): spec groups and pane sections.\n- **Body** (Geist 400, 15px / 1.5, tabular numerals): reading text, kept to 64–72ch.\n- **Label** (Geist 600, 11px, 0.14–0.16em, uppercase): row keys, tabs, buttons, captions. The floor is 11px.\n\n### Named Rules\n**The Chapter Rule.** A screen's subject is said once, large and uppercase, with a tracked index line above it only when the index carries information (Stage 4 of 9).\n\n## Layout\n\n- The brief is two columns: a sticky title column (headline and plot drawing) and the specification sheet, a run of rows with a 9.5rem key column and hairline separators. A sticky action bar ends the sheet.\n- The run is the 3D board full bleed, with the chapter caption bottom left, controls top right, a 320px scores column on the right and a 2px progress line along the bottom edge.\n- The review is the drawing stage and a 360px side panel: score, a 2×2 stats grid, the committee, the brief collapsed.\n- Gutter clamp(16px, 3.2vw, 48px); rows 16px; groups 40–64px apart.\n- Breakpoints: 1180px (narrower side panel), 980px (brief and review stack), 760px (single-column rows, full-width primary button, segmented control as a grid).\n\n## Elevation & Depth\n\nFlat, in tones. Depth comes from the ink, coal and soot steps and from vignettes, not shadows. The only shadows are the soft drop under a drawing on the plate and under floating dialogs, toasts and bubbles (0 12–40px blur, black).\n\n## Shapes\n\nPills (999px) for every control, 6px cells in the road picker, a 14px frame for the drop zone, 16px for dialogs. Lines are 1px; in the report, a 1px inset rule on the left marks a finding's severity instead of a coloured border.\n\n## Components\n\n### Buttons\n- **Primary** (`.btn--cream`): cream pill, ink label text, an arrow that moves 4px on hover. 56px on the brief, 40px elsewhere.\n- **Line** (`.btn--line`): transparent pill with a 1px rule outline that brightens on hover.\n- **Quiet** (`.btn--quiet`): label text only, for drawing tools.\n\n### Chips\n- **Toggles** (`.amenity-chip`): outlined pills; a checked toggle fills cream with ink text.\n- **Segmented** (`.seg`): a pill track; the chosen option fills cream.\n\n### Inputs / Fields\n- **Number and text**: borderless with a 1px underline that brightens on hover and turns cream on focus; numbers at 24px; units in small cream-3 text beside them; − and + steppers as outlined circles.\n- **Select**: same underline, with a drawn cream chevron.\n\n### Navigation\n- The bar: wordmark left, scheme pills centre, view tabs and actions right. A tab is selected by a cream underline that draws in from the left.\n\n### The live brief\nThe headline rewrites itself from the inputs, and the plot drawing redraws to scale with smooth geometry transitions: boundary, dashed setback envelope, road band, stacked floors, dimensions, north point.\n\n### The 3D studio\nCollectible-style figures on a warm black board: hard hats, blazers, rolled plans, clipboards. Speech bubbles in coal with a pigment label; the team's replies in cream. The drone camera holds the floor being drawn.\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n### Do:\n- **Do** set the subject of each screen large, uppercase and once.\n- **Do** separate with hairlines and space before reaching for a container.\n- **Do** keep numbers tabular and labels at 11px or larger.\n- **Do** keep red for failure only.\n\n### Don't:\n- **Don't** add cards, glass, glow, gradient text or coloured borders thicker than 1px.\n- **Don't** put a kicker or eyebrow label above a heading.\n- **Don't** use emoji or Unicode glyphs as icons; draw them in a 1.5px stroke.\n- **Don't** bring back the navy, gold-on-black or starfield looks of the earlier studio.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2742,"cache_read_input_tokens":557069,"output_tokens":7463,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2742,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7463,"cache_read_input_tokens":557069,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2742,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2742},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01951G5VPtvsmEq7HTfyVDLM":{"file_path":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\DESIGN.md","content":"---\nname: Atri Arch Studio\ndescription: A studio of architects and thirteen specialists, in the Studio Rabbit world of warm black, cream and grain.\ncolors:\n  ink: \"#0b0a09\"\n  coal: \"#141312\"\n  soot: \"#1a1919\"\n  cream: \"#ede6dc\"\n  cream-2: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.74)\"\n  cream-3: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.5)\"\n  cream-4: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.3)\"\n  rule: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.1)\"\n  rule-2: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.2)\"\n  brick: \"#c4553f\"\n  stone: \"#a39c92\"\n  sand: \"#c9b497\"\n  pale-cream: \"#e8dcc6\"\ntypography:\n  display:\n    fontFamily: \"Archivo, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"\n    fontSize: \"clamp(46px, 6.2vw, 96px)\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: 0.92\n    letterSpacing: \"-0.025em\"\n    fontVariation: \"'wdth' 94\"\n  soft:\n    fontFamily: \"Archivo, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"\n    fontSize: \"clamp(26px, 2.9vw, 46px)\"\n    fontWeight: 300\n    lineHeight: 1.05\n    letterSpacing: \"-0.01em\"\n  headline:\n    fontFamily: \"Archivo, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"\n    fontSize: \"30px\"\n    fontWeight: 500\n    lineHeight: 1\n    letterSpacing: \"-0.01em\"\n  body:\n    fontFamily: \"Geist, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"\n    fontSize: \"15px\"\n    fontWeight: 400\n    lineHeight: 1.5\n  label:\n    fontFamily: \"Geist, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"\n    fontSize: \"11px\"\n    fontWeight: 600\n    letterSpacing: \"0.14em\"\nrounded:\n  pill: \"999px\"\n  panel: \"16px\"\n  frame: \"14px\"\n  cell: \"6px\"\nspacing:\n  gutter: \"clamp(16px, 3.2vw, 48px)\"\n  row: \"16px\"\n  group: \"clamp(40px, 6vh, 64px)\"\ncomponents:\n  button-primary:\n    backgroundColor: \"{colors.cream}\"\n    textColor: \"{colors.ink}\"\n    typography: \"{typography.label}\"\n    rounded: \"{rounded.pill}\"\n    height: \"56px\"\n    padding: \"0 30px\"\n  button-line:\n    backgroundColor: \"transparent\"\n    textColor: \"{colors.cream}\"\n    rounded: \"{rounded.pill}\"\n    height: \"40px\"\n    padding: \"0 20px\"\n  toggle-on:\n    backgroundColor: \"{colors.cream}\"\n    textColor: \"{colors.ink}\"\n    rounded: \"{rounded.pill}\"\n    padding: \"8px 15px\"\n  input-underline:\n    backgroundColor: \"transparent\"\n    textColor: \"{colors.cream}\"\n    padding: \"2px 0 4px\"\n---\n\n# Design System: Atri Arch Studio\n\n## Overview\n\n**Creative North Star: \"The Studio After Dark\"**\n\nThe studio runs in the Studio Rabbit world: a warm black room, cream type, the grain of film over everything, and nothing that glows. Content is set the way that site sets its chapters: what matters goes large, uppercase and tight in Archivo, the soft line beside it in Archivo italic, and everything you operate in quiet Geist. The brief is the project's title, so the first screen is the house being asked for, typeset and drawn to scale as you type.\n\nStructure comes from hairline rules, not boxes. There are no cards, no glass panels and no gradients standing in for depth. Colour is almost absent: cream at four strengths does the work, a few warm neutrals tell disciplines apart, and one brick red means something is wrong.\n\n**Key Characteristics:**\n- Warm black ground, cream type, animated film grain at 6%.\n- Archivo uppercase display with an italic soft line; Geist for UI and tracked uppercase labels.\n- Hairline rules and pill controls; cream-filled selection.\n- Brick red is the only signal colour.\n- One authored moment per screen: the self-drawing brief, the 3D studio at work, the drawing that carries into the review.\n\n## Colors\n\nA warm monochrome: black with a little brown in it, cream with a little paper in it.\n\n### Primary\n- **Cream** (#ede6dc): all primary text, the primary button, selected toggles and tabs, line work in drawings and the 3D board.\n\n### Neutral\n- **Ink** (#0b0a09): the ground everywhere, and the 3D board's clear colour.\n- **Coal** (#141312) and **Soot** (#1a1919): raised surfaces only: dialogs, toasts, speech bubbles, the drawing sheet.\n- **Cream at 74 / 50 / 30%**: secondary text, labels, faint captions. **Rules at 10 / 20%**: every divider and control outline.\n- **Stone** (#a39c92), **Sand** (#c9b497), **Pale cream** (#e8dcc6): discipline marks (analysis, structure and cost, judgement and Vastu), mandala quarters and the airflow ramp's upper end. They are tones, never fills of a region.\n\n### Tertiary\n- **Brick** (#c4553f): breaches, critical findings, low scores, a sealed room in the airflow diagram, the toast dot. Nothing decorative.\n\n### Named Rules\n**The One Signal Rule.** Brick red appears only where something fails. If a screen shows red, it is telling you about a problem.\n\n## Typography\n\n**Display Font:** Archivo (variable, width 94%), self-hosted.\n**Body Font:** Geist (variable), self-hosted. Both are taken from the Studio Rabbit site.\n\n### Hierarchy\n- **Display** (500, clamp(46px, 6.2vw, 96px), line-height 0.92, -0.025em, uppercase): the brief headline's hard lines, the run's stage word, the review score (84px).\n- **Soft** (Archivo italic 300, clamp(26px, 2.9vw, 46px)): the brief headline's soft lines, the run title, spoken narration in the 3D tab.\n- **Headline** (Archivo 500, 30px, uppercase): spec groups and pane sections.\n- **Body** (Geist 400, 15px / 1.5, tabular numerals): reading text, kept to 64–72ch.\n- **Label** (Geist 600, 11px, 0.14–0.16em, uppercase): row keys, tabs, buttons, captions. The floor is 11px.\n\n### Named Rules\n**The Chapter Rule.** A screen's subject is said once, large and uppercase, with a tracked index line above it only when the index carries information (Stage 4 of 9).\n\n## Layout\n\n- The brief is two columns: a sticky title column (headline and plot drawing) and the specification sheet, a run of rows with a 9.5rem key column and hairline separators. A sticky action bar ends the sheet.\n- The run is the 3D board full bleed, with the chapter caption bottom left, controls top right, a 320px scores column on the right and a 2px progress line along the bottom edge.\n- The review is the drawing stage and a 360px side panel: score, a 2×2 stats grid, the committee, the brief collapsed.\n- Gutter clamp(16px, 3.2vw, 48px); rows 16px; groups 40–64px apart.\n- Breakpoints: 1180px (narrower side panel), 980px (brief and review stack), 760px (single-column rows, full-width primary button, segmented control as a grid).\n\n## Elevation & Depth\n\nFlat, in tones. Depth comes from the ink, coal and soot steps and from vignettes, not shadows. The only shadows are the soft drop under a drawing on the plate and under floating dialogs, toasts and bubbles (0 12–40px blur, black).\n\n## Shapes\n\nPills (999px) for every control, 6px cells in the road picker, a 14px frame for the drop zone, 16px for dialogs. Lines are 1px; in the report, a 1px inset rule on the left marks a finding's severity instead of a coloured border.\n\n## Components\n\n### Buttons\n- **Primary** (`.btn--cream`): cream pill, ink label text, an arrow that moves 4px on hover. 56px on the brief, 40px elsewhere.\n- **Line** (`.btn--line`): transparent pill with a 1px rule outline that brightens on hover.\n- **Quiet** (`.btn--quiet`): label text only, for drawing tools.\n\n### Chips\n- **Toggles** (`.amenity-chip`): outlined pills; a checked toggle fills cream with ink text.\n- **Segmented** (`.seg`): a pill track; the chosen option fills cream.\n\n### Inputs / Fields\n- **Number and text**: borderless with a 1px underline that brightens on hover and turns cream on focus; numbers at 24px; units in small cream-3 text beside them; − and + steppers as outlined circles.\n- **Select**: same underline, with a drawn cream chevron.\n\n### Navigation\n- The bar: wordmark left, scheme pills centre, view tabs and actions right. A tab is selected by a cream underline that draws in from the left.\n\n### The live brief\nThe headline rewrites itself from the inputs, and the plot drawing redraws to scale with smooth geometry transitions: boundary, dashed setback envelope, road band, stacked floors, dimensions, north point.\n\n### The 3D studio\nCollectible-style figures on a warm black board: hard hats, blazers, rolled plans, clipboards. Speech bubbles in coal with a pigment label; the team's replies in cream. The drone camera holds the floor being drawn.\n\n## Do's and Don'ts\n\n### Do:\n- **Do** set the subject of each screen large, uppercase and once.\n- **Do** separate with hairlines and space before reaching for a container.\n- **Do** keep numbers tabular and labels at 11px or larger.\n- **Do** keep red for failure only.\n\n### Don't:\n- **Don't** add cards, glass, glow, gradient text or coloured borders thicker than 1px.\n- **Don't** put a kicker or eyebrow label above a heading.\n- **Don't** use emoji or Unicode glyphs as icons; draw them in a 1.5px stroke.\n- **Don't** bring back the navy, gold-on-black or starfield looks of the earlier studio.\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfsFYkHJku2PA6iGu1Lat","attributionSkill":"impeccable","type":"assistant","uuid":"2f65defe-ce59-403a-be9a-04f20d04b092","timestamp":"2026-10-09T19:56:28.051Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"2f65defe-ce59-403a-be9a-04f20d04b092","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cde90b88-60f3-4a8e-aba6-b51e470ae5ea","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01951G5VPtvsmEq7HTfyVDLM","type":"tool_result","content":"The file F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\DESIGN.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"e24c8f0a-431c-464c-9255-ad2defcba398","timestamp":"2026-10-09T19:56:28.810Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"update","filePath":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\DESIGN.md","content":"","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":94,"newStart":1,"newLines":185,"lines":["-﻿# DESIGN.md — Atri Arch (Architect Intelligence Studio)","+---","+name: Atri Arch Studio","+description: A studio of architects and thirteen specialists, in the Studio Rabbit world of warm black, cream and grain.","+colors:","+  ink: \"#0b0a09\"","+  coal: \"#141312\"","+  soot: \"#1a1919\"","+  cream: \"#ede6dc\"","+  cream-2: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.74)\"","+  cream-3: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.5)\"","+  cream-4: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.3)\"","+  rule: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.1)\"","+  rule-2: \"rgba(237, 230, 220, 0.2)\"","+  brick: \"#c4553f\"","+  stone: \"#a39c92\"","+  sand: \"#c9b497\"","+  pale-cream: \"#e8dcc6\"","+typography:","+  display:","+    fontFamily: \"Archivo, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"","+    fontSize: \"clamp(46px, 6.2vw, 96px)\"","+    fontWeight: 500","+    lineHeight: 0.92","+    letterSpacing: \"-0.025em\"","+    fontVariation: \"'wdth' 94\"","+  soft:","+    fontFamily: \"Archivo, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"","+    fontSize: \"clamp(26px, 2.9vw, 46px)\"","+    fontWeight: 300","+    lineHeight: 1.05","+    letterSpacing: \"-0.01em\"","+  headline:","+    fontFamily: \"Archivo, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"","+    fontSize: \"30px\"","+    fontWeight: 500","+    lineHeight: 1","+    letterSpacing: \"-0.01em\"","+  body:","+    fontFamily: \"Geist, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"","+    fontSize: \"15px\"","+    fontWeight: 400","+    lineHeight: 1.5","+  label:","+    fontFamily: \"Geist, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\"","+    fontSize: \"11px\"","+    fontWeight: 600","+    letterSpacing: \"0.14em\"","+rounded:","+  pill: \"999px\"","+  panel: \"16px\"","+  frame: \"14px\"","+  cell: \"6px\"","+spacing:","+  gutter: \"clamp(16px, 3.2vw, 48px)\"","+  row: \"16px\"","+  group: \"clamp(40px, 6vh, 64px)\"","+components:","+  button-primary:","+    backgroundColor: \"{colors.cream}\"","+    textColor: \"{colors.ink}\"","+    typography: \"{typography.label}\"","+    rounded: \"{rounded.pill}\"","+    height: \"56px\"","+    padding: \"0 30px\"","+  button-line:","+    backgroundColor: \"transparent\"","+    textColor: \"{colors.cream}\"","+    rounded: \"{rounded.pill}\"","+    height: \"40px\"","+    padding: \"0 20px\"","+  toggle-on:","+    backgroundColor: \"{colors.cream}\"","+    textColor: \"{colors.ink}\"","+    rounded: \"{rounded.pill}\"","+    padding: \"8px 15px\"","+  input-underline:","+    backgroundColor: \"transparent\"","+    textColor: \"{colors.cream}\"","+    padding: \"2px 0 4px\"","+---"," ","-Documenting the modern **Pitch-Black Cosmic Space & Architectural CAD** design system.  ","-Ground truth is `frontend/index.html`, `frontend/studio.css`, `frontend/studio.js`, and `frontend/classic.html`.","+# Design System: Atri Arch Studio"," ","----","+## Overview"," ","-## 1. Design Vision & Philosophy","+**Creative North Star: \"The Studio After Dark\"**"," ","-**Pitch-Black Cosmic Space meets Precision Architectural CAD.**","+The studio runs in the Studio Rabbit world: a warm black room, cream type, the grain of film over everything, and nothing that glows. Content is set the way that site sets its chapters: what matters goes large, uppercase and tight in Archivo, the soft line beside it in Archivo italic, and everything you operate in quiet Geist. The brief is the project's title, so the first screen is the house being asked for, typeset and drawn to scale as you type."," ","-Atri Arch presents an autonomous multi-agent architectural studio as a fusion of cosmic infinity and mathematical drafting precision. The experience opens with an animated architectural blueprint drafting sequence before expanding into a pitch-black workspace illuminated by starlight, glassmorphism cards, and laser-precise typography.","+Structure comes from hairline rules, not boxes. There are no cards, no glass panels and no gradients standing in for depth. Colour is almost absent: cream at four strengths does the work, a few warm neutrals tell disciplines apart, and one brick red means something is wrong."," ","-### Refused by Construction:","-- Artificial Intelligence \"slop\" emojis (📐, 🏡, ✨, 🤖)","-- Generic dark blue / navy gradients — the ground is **pure `#000000` pitch black**","-- Cluttered chrome or low-contrast text","-- Sluggish heavy CSS filter blurs that stutter frame rates","+**Key Characteristics:**","+- Warm black ground, cream type, animated film grain at 6%.","+- Archivo uppercase display with an italic soft line; Geist for UI and tracked uppercase labels.","+- Hairline rules and pill controls; cream-filled selection.","+- Brick red is the only signal colour.","+- One authored moment per screen: the self-drawing brief, the 3D studio at work, the drawing that carries into the review."," ","----","+## Colors"," ","-## 2. Color System & Design Tokens","+A warm monochrome: black with a little brown in it, cream with a little paper in it."," ","-### The Pure Pitch-Black Universe Palette","-The base is solid `#000000`, accented with frosted glass surfaces and crisp starlight:","+### Primary","+- **Cream** (#ede6dc): all primary text, the primary button, selected toggles and tabs, line work in drawings and the 3D board."," ","-| Token | Value | Role |","-|---|---|---|","-| `--bg-base` | `#000000` | Pure pitch-black canvas and page background |","-| `--bg-card` | `rgba(8, 10, 15, 0.76)` | Frosted glassmorphic card fill |","-| `--bg-card-hover` | `rgba(14, 18, 26, 0.88)` | Card hover lift fill |","-| `--bg-input` | `rgba(5, 6, 9, 0.85)` | Inset input field surface |","-| `--bg-glass` | `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03)` | Subtle glass translucent highlights |","-| `--rule` | `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08)` | Micro hairline dividers |","-| `--rule-2` | `rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14)` | Card and interactive border lines |","-| `--rule-focus` | `#7FA3D4` | Focused input border glow |","+### Neutral","+- **Ink** (#0b0a09): the ground everywhere, and the 3D board's clear colour.","+- **Coal** (#141312) and **Soot** (#1a1919): raised surfaces only: dialogs, toasts, speech bubbles, the drawing sheet.","+- **Cream at 74 / 50 / 30%**: secondary text, labels, faint captions. **Rules at 10 / 20%**: every divider and control outline.","+- **Stone** (#a39c92), **Sand** (#c9b497), **Pale cream** (#e8dcc6): discipline marks (analysis, structure and cost, judgement and Vastu), mandala quarters and the airflow ramp's upper end. They are tones, never fills of a region."," ","-### Typography & Starlight Tones","-| Token | Value | Usage |","-|---|---|---|","-| `--chalk` | `#FFFFFF` | Primary headlines, active icons, drawn laser strokes |","-| `--chalk-2` | `#E4E7EC` | Body text, titles, labels |","-| `--chalk-3` | `#8D94A5` | Dimension text, secondary copy, input placeholders |","-| `--chalk-4` | `#474D5A` | CAD HUD metadata, tertiary indicators |","+### Tertiary","+- **Brick** (#c4553f): breaches, critical findings, low scores, a sealed room in the airflow diagram, the toast dot. Nothing decorative."," ","-### Semantic Architectural Pigments","-| Token | Value | Role & Meaning |","-|---|---|---|","-| `--indigo` | `#7FA3D4` | Computed analysis, active selections, focus highlights |","-| `--ochre` | `#E5A958` | Golden ratio guides, solar angle rays, mass & cost |","-| `--hingula` | `#F06548` | Compliance breach, structural warning, Agneya (SE) fire |","-| `--orpiment` | `#F3D063` | Vastu judgement, Vayavya (NW) air |","-| `--ok` | `#3DD68C` | Live status beacon, confirmed pass |","+### Named Rules","+**The One Signal Rule.** Brick red appears only where something fails. If a screen shows red, it is telling you about a problem."," ","----","+## Typography"," ","-## 3. Typography Stack","+**Display Font:** Archivo (variable, width 94%), self-hosted.","+**Body Font:** Geist (variable), self-hosted. Both are taken from the Studio Rabbit site."," ","-Apple-inspired geometric precision typography:","-- **Prose & UI**: `Inter`, `-apple-system`, `BlinkMacSystemFont`, `\"SF Pro Display\"`, `\"SF Pro Text\"`, `sans-serif`","-- **Telemetry & Dimensions**: `JetBrains Mono`, `ui-monospace`, `\"SF Mono\"`, `\"Cascadia Code\"`, `monospace`","+### Hierarchy","+- **Display** (500, clamp(46px, 6.2vw, 96px), line-height 0.92, -0.025em, uppercase): the brief headline's hard lines, the run's stage word, the review score (84px).","+- **Soft** (Archivo italic 300, clamp(26px, 2.9vw, 46px)): the brief headline's soft lines, the run title, spoken narration in the 3D tab.","+- **Headline** (Archivo 500, 30px, uppercase): spec groups and pane sections.","+- **Body** (Geist 400, 15px / 1.5, tabular numerals): reading text, kept to 64–72ch.","+- **Label** (Geist 600, 11px, 0.14–0.16em, uppercase): row keys, tabs, buttons, captions. The floor is 11px."," ","-**Rule**: All architectural numbers, coordinates, areas, and currency figures use monospaced digits with `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums` to prevent layout shift during updates.","+### Named Rules","+**The Chapter Rule.** A screen's subject is said once, large and uppercase, with a tracked index line above it only when the index carries information (Stage 4 of 9)."," ","----","+## Layout"," ","-## 4. Key Architectural Sequences","+- The brief is two columns: a sticky title column (headline and plot drawing) and the specification sheet, a run of rows with a 9.5rem key column and hairline separators. A sticky action bar ends the sheet.","+- The run is the 3D board full bleed, with the chapter caption bottom left, controls top right, a 320px scores column on the right and a 2px progress line along the bottom edge.","+- The review is the drawing stage and a 360px side panel: score, a 2×2 stats grid, the committee, the brief collapsed.","+- Gutter clamp(16px, 3.2vw, 48px); rows 16px; groups 40–64px apart.","+- Breakpoints: 1180px (narrower side panel), 980px (brief and review stack), 760px (single-column rows, full-width primary button, segmented control as a grid)."," ","-### A. The Architectural Blueprint CAD Intro","-When the studio loads, an SVG blueprint drafting sequence renders on a pitch-black screen:","-1. **CAD HUD Telemetry**: `CAD // SYS.REV-04`, `SCALE 1:100`, `AZIMUTH 042° NE`, `13 CRITICS ONLINE` with a pulsing status beacon.","-2. **Drafting Compass & Golden Ratio**: Fibonacci spiral arcs and solar rays (`SOLAR 45°`) sketch out.","-3. **3D Isometric Pavilion**: Cantilevered slab, structural pilotis, floating roof pergola, and a 9×9 sacred Vastu module floor grid.","-4. **Dimension Annotations**: Precision leader lines with extension ticks (`18.00 m`, `12.00 m`, `EL +6.80`).","-5. **Brand Stroke Etch**: Laser-stroke drawing of **`ATRI · ARCH`** with subtext and live status ticker.","-6. **Auto-Dismiss & Skip**: Seamlessly transitions after 2.8s or immediately upon clicking **Enter Studio →**.","+## Elevation & Depth"," ","-### B. The Cosmic Star-Field Engine (`space-stars`)","-A high-performance Canvas 2D starfield runs across 3 phases:","-1. **Forming (Intro Phase)**: 240 stars materialize in a rotating galaxy cluster around the architectural CAD center.","-2. **Spreading (Transition Phase)**: As the intro dismisses, stars expand outward with smooth exponential easing `(s.x += (targetX - s.x) * 0.055)` across the entire home page.","-3. **Ambient (Home Page Phase)**: Stars drift with gentle sine-wave twinkling and interactive mouse repulsion.","+Flat, in tones. Depth comes from the ink, coal and soot steps and from vignettes, not shadows. The only shadows are the soft drop under a drawing on the plate and under floating dialogs, toasts and bubbles (0 12–40px blur, black)."," ","----","+## Shapes"," ","-## 5. UI Architecture & Comparison Tool","+Pills (999px) for every control, 6px cells in the road picker, a 14px frame for the drop zone, 16px for dialogs. Lines are 1px; in the report, a 1px inset rule on the left marks a finding's severity instead of a coloured border."," ","-### Three Phase Flow:","-- `body[data-phase=\"compose\"]`: Modern glassmorphic brief composition cards with live plot dimension & area stats.","-- `body[data-phase=\"running\"]`: Autonomous multi-critic synthesis tracker with live stage indicators.","-- `body[data-phase=\"review\"]`: 8 diagnostic views (Drawings, Mandala, Vastu, Cost, Interior, 3D, Findings, Audit).","+## Components"," ","-### Classic UI Comparison System:","-- A dedicated **`Compare UI`** button in the header opens a side-by-side modal displaying the original classic layout (`classic.html`) next to the new modern design for real-time evaluation.","\\ No newline at end of file","+### Buttons","+- **Primary** (`.btn--cream`): cream pill, ink label text, an arrow that moves 4px on hover. 56px on the brief, 40px elsewhere.","+- **Line** (`.btn--line`): transparent pill with a 1px rule outline that brightens on hover.","+- **Quiet** (`.btn--quiet`): label text only, for drawing tools.","+","+### Chips","+- **Toggles** (`.amenity-chip`): outlined pills; a checked toggle fills cream with ink text.","+- **Segmented** (`.seg`): a pill track; the chosen option fills cream.","+","+### Inputs / Fields","+- **Number and text**: borderless with a 1px underline that brightens on hover and turns cream on focus; numbers at 24px; units in small cream-3 text beside them; − and + steppers as outlined circles.","+- **Select**: same underline, with a drawn cream chevron.","+","+### Navigation","+- The bar: wordmark left, scheme pills centre, view tabs and actions right. A tab is selected by a cream underline that draws in from the left.","+","+### The live brief","+The headline rewrites itself from the inputs, and the plot drawing redraws to scale with smooth geometry transitions: boundary, dashed setback envelope, road band, stacked floors, dimensions, north point.","+","+### The 3D studio","+Collectible-style figures on a warm black board: hard hats, blazers, rolled plans, clipboards. Speech bubbles in coal with a pigment label; the team's replies in cream. The drone camera holds the floor being drawn.","+","+## Do's and Don'ts","+","+### Do:","+- **Do** set the subject of each screen large, uppercase and once.","+- **Do** separate with hairlines and space before reaching for a container.","+- **Do** keep numbers tabular and labels at 11px or larger.","+- **Do** keep red for failure only.","+","+### Don't:","+- **Don't** add cards, glass, glow, gradient text or coloured borders thicker than 1px.","+- **Don't** put a kicker or eyebrow label above a heading.","+- **Don't** use emoji or Unicode glyphs as icons; draw them in a 1.5px stroke.","+- **Don't** bring back the navy, gold-on-black or starfield looks of the earlier studio."]}],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2f65defe-ce59-403a-be9a-04f20d04b092","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.293","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"e24c8f0a-431c-464c-9255-ad2defcba398","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfsFYkmaCj62bxYqB9rSX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012BR3PKH8gDLjzamSXwFAFE","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\.impeccable\\design.json","content":"{\n  \"schemaVersion\": 2,\n  \"generatedAt\": \"2026-10-10T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"title\": \"Design System: Atri Arch Studio\",\n  \"extensions\": {\n    \"colorMeta\": {\n      \"ink\": { \"role\": \"neutral\", \"displayName\": \"Warm Ink\", \"canonical\": \"#0b0a09\", \"tonalRamp\": [\"#0b0a09\", \"#141312\", \"#1a1919\", \"#2a2724\", \"#57524b\", \"#8a847b\", \"#c2bbb1\", \"#ede6dc\"] },\n      \"cream\": { \"role\": \"primary\", \"displayName\": \"Paper Cream\", \"canonical\": \"#ede6dc\", \"tonalRamp\": [\"#3b3833\", \"#57524b\", \"#77716a\", \"#9a948b\", \"#bdb6ac\", \"#d7d0c6\", \"#ede6dc\", \"#f8f4ee\"] },\n      \"brick\": { \"role\": \"tertiary\", \"displayName\": \"Brick Signal\", \"canonical\": \"#c4553f\", \"tonalRamp\": [\"#3a1610\", \"#5e2419\", \"#833324\", \"#a74430\", \"#c4553f\", \"#d47866\", \"#e3a193\", \"#f1cdc5\"] },\n      \"stone\": { \"role\": \"neutral\", \"displayName\": \"Stone\", \"canonical\": \"#a39c92\" },\n      \"sand\": { \"role\": \"neutral\", \"displayName\": \"Sand\", \"canonical\": \"#c9b497\" },\n      \"pale-cream\": { \"role\": \"neutral\", \"displayName\": \"Pale Cream\", \"canonical\": \"#e8dcc6\" }\n    },\n    \"typographyMeta\": {\n      \"display\": { \"displayName\": \"Display\", \"purpose\": \"The one large uppercase statement per screen.\" },\n      \"soft\": { \"displayName\": \"Soft line\", \"purpose\": \"Archivo italic beside or above the display line.\" },\n      \"label\": { \"displayName\": \"Label\", \"purpose\": \"Row keys, tabs, buttons and captions; never under 11px.\" }\n    },\n    \"shadows\": [\n      { \"name\": \"float\", \"value\": \"0 12px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.5)\", \"purpose\": \"Speech bubbles, toasts and dialogs floating over the board.\" },\n      { \"name\": \"sheet\", \"value\": \"drop-shadow(0 24px 48px rgba(0,0,0,0.55))\", \"purpose\": \"A drawing resting on the plate.\" }\n    ],\n    \"motion\": [\n      { \"name\": \"ease-out\", \"value\": \"cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)\", \"purpose\": \"Every reveal, underline draw and geometry change.\" },\n      { \"name\": \"ease-in-out\", \"value\": \"cubic-bezier(0.87, 0, 0.13, 1)\", \"purpose\": \"Looping cues such as the engine beat.\" },\n      { \"name\": \"grain\", \"value\": \"1.2s steps(6) infinite\", \"purpose\": \"Film grain over the whole page.\" }\n    ],\n    \"breakpoints\": [\n      { \"name\": \"narrow-side\", \"value\": \"1180px\" },\n      { \"name\": \"stack\", \"value\": \"980px\" },\n      { \"name\": \"phone\", \"value\": \"760px\" }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"components\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Primary Button\", \"kind\": \"button\", \"refersTo\": \"button-primary\",\n      \"description\": \"The one action that moves the work forward.\",\n      \"html\": \"<button class=\\\"ds-btn\\\">Convene the studio <svg viewBox=\\\"0 0 24 24\\\"><path d=\\\"M4 12h15M13 6l6 6-6 6\\\"/></svg></button>\",\n      \"css\": \".ds-btn { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:12px; height:56px; padding:0 30px; border:0; border-radius:999px; background:#ede6dc; color:#0b0a09; font:600 12px Geist, Helvetica, sans-serif; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; cursor:pointer; transition:background-color .3s; } .ds-btn svg { width:16px; height:16px; fill:none; stroke:currentColor; stroke-width:1.6; transition:transform .45s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1); } .ds-btn:hover { background:#fff; } .ds-btn:hover svg { transform:translateX(4px); } .ds-btn:focus-visible { outline:1px solid #ede6dc; outline-offset:3px; }\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Line Button\", \"kind\": \"button\", \"refersTo\": \"button-line\",\n      \"description\": \"Secondary actions: cancel, new brief.\",\n      \"html\": \"<button class=\\\"ds-line\\\">Cancel</button>\",\n      \"css\": \".ds-line { height:40px; padding:0 20px; border:0; border-radius:999px; background:transparent; color:#ede6dc; box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(237,230,220,.2); font:600 11px Geist, Helvetica, sans-serif; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; cursor:pointer; } .ds-line:hover { box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(237,230,220,.5); } .ds-line:focus-visible { outline:1px solid #ede6dc; outline-offset:3px; }\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Toggle\", \"kind\": \"chip\", \"refersTo\": \"toggle-on\",\n      \"description\": \"A room or option that is in or out.\",\n      \"html\": \"<span class=\\\"ds-chip\\\">Study</span> <span class=\\\"ds-chip is-on\\\">Pooja room</span>\",\n      \"css\": \".ds-chip { display:inline-block; padding:8px 15px; border-radius:999px; font:400 13px Geist, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:rgba(237,230,220,.74); box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(237,230,220,.2); } .ds-chip:hover { color:#ede6dc; } .ds-chip.is-on { background:#ede6dc; color:#0b0a09; box-shadow:none; }\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Underline Number\", \"kind\": \"input\", \"refersTo\": \"input-underline\",\n      \"description\": \"A quantity in the specification sheet.\",\n      \"html\": \"<label class=\\\"ds-num\\\"><input value=\\\"12\\\"><i>m wide</i></label>\",\n      \"css\": \".ds-num { display:inline-flex; align-items:baseline; gap:8px; } .ds-num input { width:4.6ch; border:0; border-bottom:1px solid rgba(237,230,220,.2); background:transparent; color:#ede6dc; font:400 24px Geist, Helvetica, sans-serif; } .ds-num input:focus { outline:none; border-color:#ede6dc; } .ds-num i { font:400 13px Geist, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-style:normal; color:rgba(237,230,220,.5); }\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"View Tab\", \"kind\": \"nav\",\n      \"description\": \"Header and pane tabs: selected by an underline drawn from the left.\",\n      \"html\": \"<nav class=\\\"ds-tabs\\\"><button class=\\\"is-on\\\">Drawings</button><button>Vastu</button><button>Cost</button></nav>\",\n      \"css\": \".ds-tabs { display:flex; gap:2px; } .ds-tabs button { position:relative; height:36px; padding:0 12px; border:0; background:none; color:rgba(237,230,220,.5); font:600 11.5px Geist, Helvetica, sans-serif; letter-spacing:.14em; text-transform:uppercase; cursor:pointer; } .ds-tabs button::after { content:''; position:absolute; left:12px; right:12px; bottom:4px; height:1px; background:#ede6dc; transform:scaleX(0); transform-origin:left; transition:transform .5s cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1); } .ds-tabs button:hover, .ds-tabs .is-on { color:#ede6dc; } .ds-tabs .is-on::after { transform:scaleX(1); }\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Chapter Caption\", \"kind\": \"custom\",\n      \"description\": \"The run's stage: an informative index over one large uppercase word.\",\n      \"html\": \"<div class=\\\"ds-ch\\\"><p>Stage 4 of 9</p><h3>Review</h3><span>13 critics reviewing 3 schemes</span></div>\",\n      \"css\": \".ds-ch p { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:14px; margin:0 0 14px; font:600 11px Geist, Helvetica, sans-serif; letter-spacing:.16em; text-transform:uppercase; color:rgba(237,230,220,.74); } .ds-ch p::after { content:''; width:56px; height:1px; background:rgba(237,230,220,.5); } .ds-ch h3 { margin:0; font:500 72px/.92 Archivo, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-stretch:94%; letter-spacing:-.025em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#ede6dc; } .ds-ch span { display:block; margin-top:14px; font:400 15px Geist, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:rgba(237,230,220,.74); }\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": {\n    \"northStar\": \"The Studio After Dark\",\n    \"overview\": \"The studio runs in the Studio Rabbit world: warm black, cream type, film grain, nothing that glows. What matters is set large, uppercase and tight in Archivo with an italic soft line; everything you operate is quiet Geist. Structure comes from hairline rules, not boxes, and the only colour that speaks is brick red, for failure.\",\n    \"keyCharacteristics\": [\"Warm black ground and cream type\", \"Archivo uppercase display with an italic soft line\", \"Hairline rules and pill controls\", \"Brick red as the only signal\", \"One authored moment per screen\"],\n    \"rules\": [\n      { \"name\": \"The One Signal Rule\", \"body\": \"Brick red appears only where something fails.\", \"section\": \"colors\" },\n      { \"name\": \"The Chapter Rule\", \"body\": \"A screen's subject is said once, large and uppercase; an index line sits above it only when the index carries information.\", \"section\": \"typography\" }\n    ],\n    \"dos\": [\"Do set each screen's subject large, uppercase and once.\", \"Do separate with hairlines and space before containers.\", \"Do keep numbers tabular and labels at 11px or larger.\", \"Do keep red for failure only.\"],\n    \"donts\": [\"Don't add cards, glass, glow, gradient text or coloured borders thicker than 1px.\", \"Don't put a kicker or eyebrow above a heading.\", \"Don't use emoji or glyphs as icons.\", \"Don't bring back the navy, gold-on-black or starfield looks.\"]\n  }\n}\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2742,"cache_read_input_tokens":557069,"output_tokens":7463,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2742,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":7463,"cache_read_input_tokens":557069,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2742,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2742},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_012B