{"parentUuid":"ee24b7d0-2590-4184-8107-628465bb78c2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfsGvpDv13GdcHLUEUD5u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"When the design is ready, the team now fast-forwards through what's left instead of jumping to the end: every line is drawn and every wall rises on screen. Committed locally as `018a155`, not pushed.\n\n- **Visible fast-forward:** the team's speed is set from how much drawing is left, so the busiest figure finishes in about 5 seconds. On a test board where nothing was drawn yet, that came out at about 9× normal speed. Rooms filled in one after another (0 → 3 → 7 → all 8), and none were skipped.\n- **Built as they go:** a room's walls and windows now go up around it as soon as its outline is finished, instead of the whole house appearing at the end. In the test, all 32 wall pieces rose this way.\n- **Normal speed:** while the engine is still working, drawing is back at its previous speed. I'd slowed it down first; your follow-up made clear that wasn't what you meant.\n- **Safety net:** if a run somehow takes longer than 15 seconds after the result arrives, whatever's left is finished instantly so the review always opens. It shouldn't come into play.\n\nI tested on a sample board in the preview because the preview pauses animation, so a real run there just jumps to the end. Watch one live run in your own browser to see it at full speed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":881,"cache_read_input_tokens":588004,"output_tokens":431,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":881,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":431,"cache_read_input_tokens":588004