{"parentUuid":"529892f8-1cad-4ed4-97ba-b8fdc2bc7c42","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cde90b88-60f3-4a8e-aba6-b51e470ae5ea","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R8XAqLb1Mt69PurAYwVwU7","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a7c60aeb9036b6276 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a7c60aeb9036b6276', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: F:\\Users\\shrey\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\tasks\\a7c60aeb9036b6276.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"be45de20-7a27-4728-8b95-065dce3ac547","timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:11:13.254Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a7c60aeb9036b6276","description":"Fix floor-plan import pipeline","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"You are implementing a fix in a Python/FastAPI backend at `F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend` (Windows; use the venv: `.venv/Scripts/python.exe`). Do NOT touch the frontend, do NOT git commit or push, do NOT call paid APIs. Work only inside `backend/`.\n\n## The problem (verified)\nFloor-plan uploads only work when every room is a closed shape (the platform's own exports). Real-world files fail:\n- `var/fixtures/walls.dxf`: walls drawn as LINE pairs (wall faces) with gaps at doors, labels as MTEXT with formatting codes, units mm ($INSUNITS=4), plus a dimension line/text on layer A-DIMS → \"No closed room outlines found\".\n- `var/fixtures/walls.svg`: walls as `<line>` with stroke widths inside `<g transform=\"translate(100,100)\">`, labels as `<text>` → \"No room shapes found\".\n- `var/fixtures/scan.png` (thick walls, door gaps, text labels incl. size strings like \"4.6 x 5.0\", a dimension string \"12000\" under the plan, 1.2° rotation, noise, blur) and `var/fixtures/sketch.jpg` (thin 4px walls, washed-out, -2° rotation): image import relies ONLY on a remote free vision model which is rate-limited → fails (and blocked 58 s).\n\nFixtures are produced by `python -m scripts.import_fixtures`; the scorer is `python -m scripts.import_bench` (prints rooms / matched-by-IoU>0.5 out of 12 / correctly typed / mean IoU). Ground truth is `var/fixtures/truth.json`. Read both scripts first.\n\nRelevant code: `aip/engines/architecture/importer.py` (parse_dxf, parse_svg, parse_image, `_scale_to_plot`, `assemble`, `import_floorplan`, `classify`, `_clean_label`, ParsedRoom/ImportResult/ImportError_), `aip/api/routers/imports.py`, tests in `tests/test_import.py`. Geometry helpers in `aip/domain/geometry.py`. Installed and usable: numpy, scipy, shapely 2.1, ezdxf 1.4 (optional), Pillow, opencv-python-headless (cv2), rapidocr_onnxruntime (local CPU OCR: `from rapidocr_onnxruntime import RapidOCR; RapidOCR()(img)` returns [[box, text, score], ...]). Add opencv-python-headless and rapidocr-onnxruntime to pyproject.toml dependencies (an `[project.optional-dependencies] vision` extra is fine, but the import path must degrade gracefully with a clear message if they are missing).\n\n## What to build\n\n### 1. New module `aip/engines/architecture/recover.py`: rooms from wall linework (shared by DXF, SVG and raster)\n`rooms_from_linework(segments: list[tuple[Vec2, Vec2]], labels: list[tuple[str, Vec2]], *, door_gap: float | None = None) -> tuple[list[ParsedRoom], list[str]]`\n- Union the segments (shapely), extent E = max(width, height) of their bounds.\n- Snap tolerance s = 0.004*E; door gap g = door_gap or 0.06*E (callers pass ~1.0 in metre units when units are known).\n- walls = unary_union(lines).buffer(s); closed = morphological closing (buffer(+g/2, mitre) then buffer(-g/2, mitre)) so door gaps and double-line wall faces become a solid wall mass.\n- Rooms = the interior rings (holes) of every polygon in `closed`. Grow each by half the estimated wall thickness (estimate from double-line spacing or stroke width; fall back to 0.5*s) so neighbours share edges, then simplify (tolerance s) and rectify near-axis-aligned edges (snap edges within ~6° of an axis exactly onto it).\n- Drop faces under 1.5% of the summed face area or with min side < 0.04*E.\n- Assign labels: text whose anchor lies inside a face → that face (smallest containing). Strip DXF/MTEXT formatting (\\f...;, \\P, {}, \\H...;) and area/size tails via the existing `_clean_label`. Ignore pure numbers/dimension strings. Unlabelled faces get a heuristic type (aspect > 3 → corridor; area < 6% of total → bathroom; else bedroom) with confidence 0.4 and one warning listing how many were guessed.\n\n### 2. DXF (`parse_dxf`)\nKeep the current closed-polyline path. If it yields < 2 rooms, collect linework: LINE, LWPOLYLINE/POLYLINE (open or closed, all edges), ARC/CIRCLE skipped (door swings), INSERT ignored (furniture blocks). Use layers whose name matches /wall|mur|wand|a-wall/i if any exist, else all layers except ones matching /dim|anno|text|furn|door|hatch|grid|axis|title/i. Read $INSUNITS (1 inch, 2 foot, 4 mm, 5 cm, 6 m) to convert to metres, else keep the existing extent-based guess. Call rooms_from_linework with door_gap ≈ 1.0 m in source units.\n\n### 3. SVG (`parse_svg`)\nApply transforms properly: compose `transform` (matrix/translate/scale/rotate, multiple in one attribute) down the element tree for every shape and text; remove the \"transforms are not applied\" warning. Collect linework from `<line>`, `<polyline>`, `<polygon>`, `<rect>` (4 edges), and `<path>` (support M/L/H/V/Z absolute and relative, approximate C/Q/A by their end points). Keep the current closed-shape path first; if it yields < 2 rooms, use rooms_from_linework. Ignore elements with stroke-width under 25% of the median stroke-width when there is a clear thick/thin split (those are dimension/hatch lines).\n\n### 4. Raster images: `parse_image_local(data: bytes)` with OpenCV, used BEFORE the vision model\n1. Decode (cv2.imdecode), grayscale, normalise contrast (CLAHE), downscale so the long side ≤ 2000 px.\n2. OCR the whole image once with RapidOCR (lazy global singleton). Keep boxes + text.\n3. Deskew: dominant line angle from cv2.HoughLinesP on edges, folded to (-45, 45]; rotate image and OCR boxes by it if |angle| > 0.3°.\n4. Binary dark mask via Otsu (+ adaptive threshold fallback for washed-out images). Paint OCR text boxes white so text is not taken for walls.\n5. Wall thickness t from the distance transform (2 × median of local DT maxima ≥ 1). Wall mask = morphological opening with a ~0.7t square kernel (removes thin dimension lines/noise; for thin-wall drawings where t ≤ 5 px keep the mask and remove only small connected components instead).\n6. Close door gaps along straight walls: closing with horizontal (k×1) and vertical (1×k) line kernels, k ≈ 6% of the wall mask's bounding extent, bounded below by 3t.\n7. Rooms = connected components of the non-wall region that do not touch the image border; drop those under 1% of the building bounding-box area. Dilate each by t/2 (to wall centrelines), cv2.findContours → approxPolyDP (ε = 1% of perimeter) → rectify to axes.\n8. Scale: parse room size strings in OCR text inside rooms (\"4.6 x 5.0\", \"4.6m x 5.0m\", \"15'6\\\" x 12'0\\\"\") and estimate px-per-metre as the median ratio of the room's pixel bbox to its stated size; else parse a long dimension string (\"12000\", \"12.0 m\", \"40'-0\\\"\") near the outer extent. Return meta {\"px_per_m\", \"building_w_m\", \"building_h_m\", \"north\": \"unknown\", \"model\": \"local-cv\"}.\n9. Return rooms in the same normalised-fraction, y-up convention parse_image already uses (so assemble/_scale_to_plot keep working), with OCR labels assigned by containment and cleaned by `_clean_label`; confidence 0.85 for geometry, label confidence from OCR score.\nIn `import_floorplan`: images go to parse_image_local first; only if it returns < 2 rooms (or cv2/rapidocr are unavailable) fall back to the vision model, and give that call a 20 s timeout (asyncio.wait_for) so an upload never hangs a minute. When px_per_m is known, pass the real building size so the plan is scaled correctly even without a user-given plot size. Error messages must say what to do next.\n\n## Acceptance (run these yourself and iterate until met)\n- `python -m scripts.import_bench`: own.dxf and own.svg stay at 12/12 matched, iou ≥ 0.95. walls.dxf and walls.svg: ≥ 11/12 matched, iou ≥ 0.8, ≥ 10 correctly typed. scan.png: ≥ 10/12 matched, iou ≥ 0.75, ≥ 9 typed, under 10 s, no network call. sketch.jpg: ≥ 9/12 matched, iou ≥ 0.7, ≥ 7 typed.\n- Add tests to `tests/test_import.py` covering walls.dxf, walls.svg, scan.png and sketch.jpg built in-test via `scripts.import_fixtures` helper functions into tmp_path (no network: monkeypatch the vision router to raise if called), plus SVG transform handling and DXF $INSUNITS. Raster tests may be marked skip when cv2/rapidocr are missing.\n- Full suite passes: `.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest -q` (was 252 passing) and `-q aip/engines/vastu/calibration/test_calibration.py`.\n- Match the existing code style (docstrings explain *why*, type hints, no new frameworks).\n\nReport back: files changed, the final bench table, test counts, and anything you could not meet with the reason.","outputFile":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\tasks\\a7c60aeb9036b6276.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"529892f8-1cad-4ed4-97ba-b8fdc2bc7c42","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
