{"parentUuid":"2573b45e-3ece-4686-9a49-638908368fef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cft9ZobaWYrb56yy2KdtT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2414,"cache_read_input_tokens":708887,"output_tokens":951,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":490},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2414,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":951,"cache_read_input_tokens":708887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2414},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":9988,"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cft9ZoDWEQxRSMBJqfigw","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8907f6a5-4772-49f2-985b-be0a9a238e12","timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:18:13.579Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"8907f6a5-4772-49f2-985b-be0a9a238e12","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cft9ZobaWYrb56yy2KdtT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Progress so far:\n\n- **Uploads (agent running):** I can now reproduce every failure. Our own DXF and SVG exports import perfectly. Walls-only DXF, walls-only SVG, a scanned image and a phone photo all fail. The scan also hung for 58 seconds waiting on a rate-limited free vision model. A Sonnet agent is building the fix: room recovery from wall linework, SVG transforms applied properly, and a local OpenCV + OCR image reader that needs no network. The benchmark it has to pass is in `backend/scripts/import_bench.py`.\n- **Plan quality (measured, next task):** only 1 of 30 generated plans is defect-free. The main causes:\n  - staircases evolved separately per floor end up as much as 5.5 m apart between levels\n  - large programmes on small plots get squeezed into 1.1 m-wide bedrooms and bathrooms you reach through the kitchen\n  - bedrooms and living rooms come out as long slots, up to 5:1\n  - corridors take too much floor area\n\n  The sweep that measures this is `backend/scripts/plan_sweep.py`.\n- **Next agents, one at a time:** plan quality, then detailed 3D architecture with real materials, then interiors with 3D furniture, then a real airflow solve, then Vastu in 3D.\n\nI'll pick this up as soon as the import agent reports back."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2414,"cache_read_input_tokens":708887,"output_tokens":951,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":490},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2414,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":951,"cache_read_input_tokens":708887,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2414},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cft9ZoDWEQxRSMBJqfigw","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ff6fb32a-0f9c-430d-b58e-7e3e54f5ce25","timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:18:13.615Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"ff6fb32a-0f9c-430d-b58e-7e3e54f5ce25","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"stop_hook_summary","hookCount":3,"hookInfos":[{"command":"Design deep pass","durationMs":117},{"command":"callback"},{"command":"callback"}],"hookErrors":[],"hookAdditionalContext":[],"preventedContinuation":false,"stopReason":"","hasOutput":false,"level":"suggestion","timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:18:15.732Z","uuid":"52bccfbb-fbf9-441e-a91e-addc7db2ba8a","toolUseID":"4c17009d-901d-40f1-90f4-cc4a98fcb41a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"52bccfbb-fbf9-441e-a91e-addc7db2ba8a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c2c4d652-c039-4c0f-b2af-c6dc131ef5fd","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a7c60aeb9036b6276</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01R8XAqLb1Mt69PurAYwVwU7</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>F:\\Users\\shrey\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\tasks\\a7c60aeb9036b6276.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix floor-plan import pipeline\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All the acceptance targets are met, and the full suite passes (275 tests, up from 252) along with the 22 calibration tests.\n\n## Bench\n\nFinal `python -m scripts.import_bench`, run before the last ruff pass and the full pytest run. Both were green afterwards, and no code changed in between except a docstring edit in `raster.py`:\n\n| file | time | rooms | matched | typed | mean IoU |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| own.dxf | 0.5 s | 12 | 12/12 | 12 | 1.0 |\n| own.svg | 0.1 s | 13 | 12/12 | 10 | 1.0 |\n| walls.dxf | 0.1 s | 12 | 12/12 | 12 | 0.978 |\n| walls.svg | 0.1 s | 12 | 12/12 | 12 | 0.999 |\n| scan.png | 2.4 s | 12 | 12/12 | 12 | 0.962 |\n| sketch.jpg | 0.8 s | 12 | 12/12 | 12 | 0.942 |\n\nscan.png and sketch.jpg are read entirely locally with no network call.\n\n## Tests\n- Added 23 tests to `tests/test_import.py`: 54 pass there, 275 in the full suite. The raster tests skip if cv2 or rapidocr are missing.\n- Coverage:\n  - walls.dxf and walls.svg.\n  - Millimetre, metre, centimetre, inch and foot `$INSUNITS`, plus no header.\n  - An ARC and a block definition that must not close rooms.\n  - SVG transforms: nested translate and scale, rotate, matrix, and chained transforms.\n  - Hairline strokes ignored.\n  - A corridor beside a door.\n  - Unlabelled-room guessing and MTEXT stripping.\n  - scan.png and sketch.jpg with the vision router patched to raise.\n  - The 20 s vision timeout, the missing-vision-stack hint, and the vision-model fallback still working.\n- I also ran five extra raster variants (40 and 80 px/m, -3°, heavy noise, 3 px and 14 px walls); all matched 12/12. One of them exposed a wall-thickness bug, which is fixed.\n\n## Files\n- **New:** `aip/engines/architecture/recover.py` (rooms from wall linework) and `aip/engines/architecture/raster.py` (`parse_image_local`, OCR, deskew, scale).\n- **`importer.py`:**\n  - DXF: walls recovered from linework when the closed-outline path finds fewer than 2 rooms, `$INSUNITS` read, and block sections skipped.\n  - SVG: transforms composed down the tree, stroked walls handled, and the \"transforms not applied\" warning removed.\n  - `import_floorplan`: images try the local reader first and fall back to the vision model with a 20 s limit, `unit_scale` is passed to `assemble`, and error messages say what to do next.\n- **`pyproject.toml`:** a `vision` extra (opencv-python-headless, rapidocr-onnxruntime), the same two added to `dev`, and `pythonpath = [\".\"]` so the tests can import `scripts`.\n- **`aip/api/routers/imports.py`:** only the 502 message text changed.\n- **`tests/test_import.py`:** the new tests.\n\n## Deviations from the spec\n- **Door gaps in vector files:** I did not use the spec's morphological closing. Closing wide enough for a 1.05 m door also fills the 1.1 m corridor beside it. Filtering the fill by thickness doesn't help, because the door strip attaches to the filled corridor. Instead `recover.bridge_door_gaps` extends each free wall end along its own direction to the next line within `door_gap`. A small closing then fills the slit between a wall's two faces. Default `door_gap` is 0.09×E rather than 0.06×E, because 0.06×E (0.87 m) was narrower than the 1.05 m doors.\n- **Rooms:** they are still holes grown to the wall centreline, simplified and rectified; the grown size is the wall buffer plus half the face spacing.\n- **Raster door gaps:** the raster path does use line-kernel closings, but keeps only what is wall-thick. Horizontal and vertical fills are separate images, so a corridor fill can't merge with a door strip.\n- **Wall thickness:** the raster path uses the 30th percentile of the distance-transform ridge, not the median. With 6 px partitions and 12 px outer walls the median flipped between the two and broke one variant.\n- **`rooms_from_linework`:** it takes an extra optional `wall_thickness` keyword (the SVG stroke width).\n- **Fractions and scale:** image fractions are isotropic (divided by the longer side) so aspect ratio survives. When a scale is read, `import_floorplan` converts to metres and passes `unit_scale` to `assemble`, so a plot size isn't needed.\n- **Stale `$INSUNITS` header:** if it implies an absurd building size (outside 3–300 m), it is ignored and the extent guess is used. This keeps the existing \"mm coordinates under a metres header\" test valid.\n\n## Notes\n- **OCR quirks:** it clipped \"CORRIDOR\" to \"ORRIDO\" where the label crosses a wall, so labels get a fuzzy match to the nearest room-type keyword when the exact match fails. It also run-together \"MASTERBEDROOM\", which is split.\n- **Sketch scale:** sketch.jpg's size strings are too garbled to use, so its scale comes from the \"12000\" string and the dimension line beside it (45 px/m, exact). scan.png's scale comes from the size strings and comes out about 3% low (58.3 vs 60 px/m).\n- **Untracked files not mine:** `scripts/plan_sweep.py` appeared in the working tree during the session. `.claude/launch.json` was already modified. I didn't touch either.\n- **Nothing committed or pushed.**</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>275172</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>64</tool_uses><duration_ms>1439077</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"898fbdba-fc50-43f7-8c04-9abbc6824011","timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:35:12.217Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification","producer":"session-task","runId":"0mv222ju5-d5c9d138"},"promptSource":"system","turnOrigin":"task_notification","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
