{"parentUuid":"e82b9ea2-9cab-41f2-84c6-042ab2305869","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14925962 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a04faa06-4678-448e-a1b7-4401fd23ab28","timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:35:53.395Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14925962 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"a04faa06-4678-448e-a1b7-4401fd23ab28","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftAvjmLsd4nsdg2HGynN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0142uXKH43XXfGABZRq1m3Xs","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix generated plan quality","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are improving the floor-plan generator in a Python backend at `F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend` (Windows; always use `.venv/Scripts/python.exe`). Do NOT touch the frontend, do NOT git commit or push, no paid APIs. Work only in `backend/`.\n\n## Measured problem\n`python -m scripts.plan_sweep --n 30` generates one plan for each of 30 realistic briefs and scores client-visible defects. Baseline: **1/30 clean**. Defect frequency: too_much_corridor 20, long_room 16, stairs_misaligned 15, guardrail 13, cut_up 2. Read `scripts/plan_sweep.py` first (it builds briefs via `SimpleBriefRequest(...).to_brief()`, exactly as the API does, then `LayoutGenerator(brief, GeneratorConfig(seed=...)).generate(1)[0]`, and calls the generator's own `_sanity` guardrail). Detail from the baseline:\n- **Stairs not stacked:** multi-level plans evolve each floor separately (`LayoutGenerator._candidates` / `_worker`). The upper floor's staircase is only *softly* pulled toward the ground floor's (`_surrogate_fitness`: `penalty += 0.60 * (1 - overlap)` when `self._anchor`), so stairs land up to 5.5 m apart. A staircase that does not stack is structurally impossible.\n- **Infeasible programmes squeezed instead of handled:** 4–5 bedrooms on a 9×12 or 10×14 single-storey plot gives \"Bedroom is 1.5 m wide\", \"Bathroom is 1.1 m wide\", \"Utility is 0.4 m wide\", \"Bathroom passes through Kitchen/Garage\", \"Bedroom passes through Master Bedroom\". The generator never checks whether the programme physically fits the buildable envelope × levels.\n- **Slots:** bedrooms up to 3.3:1, living 5.3:1, dining 4.3:1 aspect ratios.\n- **Corridor share:** corridor + lobby often above 12% of a floor's area. (The sweep's threshold already excludes foyer and staircase.)\n\nKey code: `aip/engines/architecture/layout.py` (2570 lines: slicing-tree genome `Leaf`/`Split`, `realise`, `build_zoned_tree`, `Genome`, `mutate`, `crossover`, `GeneratorConfig`, `LayoutGenerator` with `generate`, `_candidates`, `_worker`, `_sanity`, `_prepare_requirements`, `_buildable_envelope`, `_evolve`, `_surrogate_fitness`, `_default_fitness`, `_realise_level`, `_assemble`, `_build_stairs`, `_place_doors`, `_repair_circulation`, `MIN_CLEAR_WIDTH`, `MIN_ROOM_DIMENSION`), `aip/engines/architecture/programme.py` (walkability), `aip/domain/brief.py`, `aip/domain/plan.py`, `aip/api/schemas.py` (`SimpleBriefRequest.to_brief`), `aip/agents/orchestrator.py` (how generation is called and how errors and advisories surface to the API/stream). Read them before changing anything; the docstrings explain the reasoning behind each choice.\n\n## What to build\n1. **Feasibility gate before evolution.** Compute the minimum floor area each level's programme needs: per room `max(min_area(type), min_clear_width(type)^2 × sensible aspect)` plus circulation and stairs, against the buildable envelope area per level. If it does not fit, resolve it in this order and record every step in `plan.metadata[\"advisories\"]` (a list of plain-English strings) so the user is told:\n   a) move rooms to an added level when the brief's FAR and height rules allow it (bedrooms go up first, public rooms stay on the ground floor, a staircase is added);\n   b) drop optional rooms in this order: study, balcony, utility, puja (fold it into an alcove note), extra bathrooms beyond one per two bedrooms plus one common;\n   c) shrink every room toward its minimum;\n   d) if it still cannot fit, raise a typed `InfeasibleBriefError` carrying a message like \"A 5-bedroom single-storey house needs about 118 m² but this plot's buildable area is 72 m². Add a floor, reduce bedrooms, or use a larger plot.\" Make sure the orchestrator and the SSE design stream turn that into a clean, visible error event, not a crash.\n   Make sure advisories reach the API response (plan metadata survives into `DesignResponse.plan`).\n2. **Stairs stack exactly.** Decide the staircase rectangle once, on the ground floor (or before evolution: a standard dog-leg about 2.4–2.7 m by 4.0–4.6 m, against a wall, adjacent to circulation), and make it a *fixed* leaf at the identical rectangle on every level. Recommended: carve it with locked prefix splits at the top of every level's slicing tree (mark those `Split`s locked so `mutate`/`crossover` never alter them), so each floor's GA only evolves the remaining region. Upper-floor lobby/corridor must touch the staircase (walkability already requires upper floors to be entered from the stair).\n3. **Room proportions.** In the surrogate and exact fitness, penalise habitable rooms past 1.6:1 steeply, and add a hard penalty past 2.2:1 for bedrooms and dining and past 2.5:1 for living, so slots never win when a better partition exists. Kitchens may go to 2.4:1 (galley). Bathrooms and utilities have minimum clear widths (bath 1.5 m, WC 1.0 m, utility 1.2 m) and a maximum of 3:1.\n4. **Less corridor.** Target corridor + lobby ≤ 10% of the floor, with a smooth penalty above it, and prefer a single short spine that every door opens off. Do not create a corridor at all when foyer + living can distribute to every room legally.\n5. Keep everything the generator already does well: zoning front to back from the road, Vastu orientation terms, walkability guardrail, deterministic seeds, and the clean-over-flawed preference in `generate`.\n\n## Acceptance (iterate until met)\n- `python -m scripts.plan_sweep --n 30`: at least **24/30 clean**, `stairs_misaligned` 0, no guardrail \"is 1.x m wide\" or \"passes through\" on any plan that was not explicitly reported infeasible (an infeasible brief that raises the typed error counts as handled, not as a defect; make the sweep catch `InfeasibleBriefError` and count it separately as \"infeasible\" and print its message).\n- Also run with `--n 60` once and report the numbers.\n- No plan takes more than 12 s to generate in the sweep (report the max).\n- Full suite passes: `.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest -q` (275 passing now) plus `-q aip/engines/vastu/calibration/test_calibration.py`. Add tests for: stairs identical across levels, the feasibility gate's escalation (added level, dropped optional room, typed error) and its advisories, the aspect caps, and the corridor share.\n- Match the existing style: docstrings explain *why*; type hints; no new dependencies.\n\nReport back: what you changed (files and approach), the before/after sweep tables for n=30 and n=60, the max generation time, test counts, and anything you could not meet with the reason."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1037,"cache_read_input_tokens":715408,"output_tokens":2718,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1037,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2718,"cache_read_input_tokens":715408,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1037,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1037},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0142uXKH43XXfGABZRq1m3Xs":{"description":"Fix generated plan quality","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":true,"prompt":"You are improving the floor-plan generator in a Python backend at `F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend` (Windows; always use `.venv/Scripts/python.exe`). Do NOT touch the frontend, do NOT git commit or push, no paid APIs. Work only in `backend/`.\n\n## Measured problem\n`python -m scripts.plan_sweep --n 30` generates one plan for each of 30 realistic briefs and scores client-visible defects. Baseline: **1/30 clean**. Defect frequency: too_much_corridor 20, long_room 16, stairs_misaligned 15, guardrail 13, cut_up 2. Read `scripts/plan_sweep.py` first (it builds briefs via `SimpleBriefRequest(...).to_brief()`, exactly as the API does, then `LayoutGenerator(brief, GeneratorConfig(seed=...)).generate(1)[0]`, and calls the generator's own `_sanity` guardrail). Detail from the baseline:\n- **Stairs not stacked:** multi-level plans evolve each floor separately (`LayoutGenerator._candidates` / `_worker`). The upper floor's staircase is only *softly* pulled toward the ground floor's (`_surrogate_fitness`: `penalty += 0.60 * (1 - overlap)` when `self._anchor`), so stairs land up to 5.5 m apart. A staircase that does not stack is structurally impossible.\n- **Infeasible programmes squeezed instead of handled:** 4–5 bedrooms on a 9×12 or 10×14 single-storey plot gives \"Bedroom is 1.5 m wide\", \"Bathroom is 1.1 m wide\", \"Utility is 0.4 m wide\", \"Bathroom passes through Kitchen/Garage\", \"Bedroom passes through Master Bedroom\". The generator never checks whether the programme physically fits the buildable envelope × levels.\n- **Slots:** bedrooms up to 3.3:1, living 5.3:1, dining 4.3:1 aspect ratios.\n- **Corridor share:** corridor + lobby often above 12% of a floor's area. (The sweep's threshold already excludes foyer and staircase.)\n\nKey code: `aip/engines/architecture/layout.py` (2570 lines: slicing-tree genome `Leaf`/`Split`, `realise`, `build_zoned_tree`, `Genome`, `mutate`, `crossover`, `GeneratorConfig`, `LayoutGenerator` with `generate`, `_candidates`, `_worker`, `_sanity`, `_prepare_requirements`, `_buildable_envelope`, `_evolve`, `_surrogate_fitness`, `_default_fitness`, `_realise_level`, `_assemble`, `_build_stairs`, `_place_doors`, `_repair_circulation`, `MIN_CLEAR_WIDTH`, `MIN_ROOM_DIMENSION`), `aip/engines/architecture/programme.py` (walkability), `aip/domain/brief.py`, `aip/domain/plan.py`, `aip/api/schemas.py` (`SimpleBriefRequest.to_brief`), `aip/agents/orchestrator.py` (how generation is called and how errors and advisories surface to the API/stream). Read them before changing anything; the docstrings explain the reasoning behind each choice.\n\n## What to build\n1. **Feasibility gate before evolution.** Compute the minimum floor area each level's programme needs: per room `max(min_area(type), min_clear_width(type)^2 × sensible aspect)` plus circulation and stairs, against the buildable envelope area per level. If it does not fit, resolve it in this order and record every step in `plan.metadata[\"advisories\"]` (a list of plain-English strings) so the user is told:\n   a) move rooms to an added level when the brief's FAR and height rules allow it (bedrooms go up first, public rooms stay on the ground floor, a staircase is added);\n   b) drop optional rooms in this order: study, balcony, utility, puja (fold it into an alcove note), extra bathrooms beyond one per two bedrooms plus one common;\n   c) shrink every room toward its minimum;\n   d) if it still cannot fit, raise a typed `InfeasibleBriefError` carrying a message like \"A 5-bedroom single-storey house needs about 118 m² but this plot's buildable area is 72 m². Add a floor, reduce bedrooms, or use a larger plot.\" Make sure the orchestrator and the SSE design stream turn that into a clean, visible error event, not a crash.\n   Make sure advisories reach the API response (plan metadata survives into `DesignResponse.plan`).\n2. **Stairs stack exactly.** Decide the staircase rectangle once, on the ground floor (or before evolution: a standard dog-leg about 2.4–2.7 m by 4.0–4.6 m, against a wall, adjacent to circulation), and make it a *fixed* leaf at the identical rectangle on every level. Recommended: carve it with locked prefix splits at the top of every level's slicing tree (mark those `Split`s locked so `mutate`/`crossover` never alter them), so each floor's GA only evolves the remaining region. Upper-floor lobby/corridor must touch the staircase (walkability already requires upper floors to be entered from the stair).\n3. **Room proportions.** In the surrogate and exact fitness, penalise habitable rooms past 1.6:1 steeply, and add a hard penalty past 2.2:1 for bedrooms and dining and past 2.5:1 for living, so slots never win when a better partition exists. Kitchens may go to 2.4:1 (galley). Bathrooms and utilities have minimum clear widths (bath 1.5 m, WC 1.0 m, utility 1.2 m) and a maximum of 3:1.\n4. **Less corridor.** Target corridor + lobby ≤ 10% of the floor, with a smooth penalty above it, and prefer a single short spine that every door opens off. Do not create a corridor at all when foyer + living can distribute to every room legally.\n5. Keep everything the generator already does well: zoning front to back from the road, Vastu orientation terms, walkability guardrail, deterministic seeds, and the clean-over-flawed preference in `generate`.\n\n## Acceptance (iterate until met)\n- `python -m scripts.plan_sweep --n 30`: at least **24/30 clean**, `stairs_misaligned` 0, no guardrail \"is 1.x m wide\" or \"passes through\" on any plan that was not explicitly reported infeasible (an infeasible brief that raises the typed error counts as handled, not as a defect; make the sweep catch `InfeasibleBriefError` and count it separately as \"infeasible\" and print its message).\n- Also run with `--n 60` once and report the numbers.\n- No plan takes more than 12 s to generate in the sweep (report the max).\n- Full suite passes: `.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest -q` (275 passing now) plus `-q aip/engines/vastu/calibration/test_calibration.py`. Add tests for: stairs identical across levels, the feasibility gate's escalation (added level, dropped optional room, typed error) and its advisories, the aspect caps, and the corridor share.\n- Match the existing style: docstrings explain *why*; type hints; no new dependencies.\n\nReport back: what you changed (files and approach), the before/after sweep tables for n=30 and n=60, the max generation time, test counts, and anything you could not meet with the reason."}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CftAvjPGFZ3NfThSAJnxg","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"18e7fd72-1dda-450e-824a-42458e97f3c0","timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:36:19.972Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"18e7fd72-1dda-450e-824a-42458e97f3c0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cde90b88-60f3-4a8e-aba6-b51e470ae5ea","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0142uXKH43XXfGABZRq1m3Xs","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: ac2ecc7f5007eff43 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'ac2ecc7f5007eff43', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: F:\\Users\\shrey\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\tasks\\ac2ecc7f5007eff43.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"5a95717b-581d-4bac-89fa-0bd1ed244e59","timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:36:20.105Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"ac2ecc7f5007eff43","description":"Fix generated plan quality","resolvedModel":"claude-sonnet-5-5","prompt":"You are improving the floor-plan generator in a Python backend at `F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend` (Windows; always use `.venv/Scripts/python.exe`). Do NOT touch the frontend, do NOT git commit or push, no paid APIs. Work only in `backend/`.\n\n## Measured problem\n`python -m scripts.plan_sweep --n 30` generates one plan for each of 30 realistic briefs and scores client-visible defects. Baseline: **1/30 clean**. Defect frequency: too_much_corridor 20, long_room 16, stairs_misaligned 15, guardrail 13, cut_up 2. Read `scripts/plan_sweep.py` first (it builds briefs via `SimpleBriefRequest(...).to_brief()`, exactly as the API does, then `LayoutGenerator(brief, GeneratorConfig(seed=...)).generate(1)[0]`, and calls the generator's own `_sanity` guardrail). Detail from the baseline:\n- **Stairs not stacked:** multi-level plans evolve each floor separately (`LayoutGenerator._candidates` / `_worker`). The upper floor's staircase is only *softly* pulled toward the ground floor's (`_surrogate_fitness`: `penalty += 0.60 * (1 - overlap)` when `self._anchor`), so stairs land up to 5.5 m apart. A staircase that does not stack is structurally impossible.\n- **Infeasible programmes squeezed instead of handled:** 4–5 bedrooms on a 9×12 or 10×14 single-storey plot gives \"Bedroom is 1.5 m wide\", \"Bathroom is 1.1 m wide\", \"Utility is 0.4 m wide\", \"Bathroom passes through Kitchen/Garage\", \"Bedroom passes through Master Bedroom\". The generator never checks whether the programme physically fits the buildable envelope × levels.\n- **Slots:** bedrooms up to 3.3:1, living 5.3:1, dining 4.3:1 aspect ratios.\n- **Corridor share:** corridor + lobby often above 12% of a floor's area. (The sweep's threshold already excludes foyer and staircase.)\n\nKey code: `aip/engines/architecture/layout.py` (2570 lines: slicing-tree genome `Leaf`/`Split`, `realise`, `build_zoned_tree`, `Genome`, `mutate`, `crossover`, `GeneratorConfig`, `LayoutGenerator` with `generate`, `_candidates`, `_worker`, `_sanity`, `_prepare_requirements`, `_buildable_envelope`, `_evolve`, `_surrogate_fitness`, `_default_fitness`, `_realise_level`, `_assemble`, `_build_stairs`, `_place_doors`, `_repair_circulation`, `MIN_CLEAR_WIDTH`, `MIN_ROOM_DIMENSION`), `aip/engines/architecture/programme.py` (walkability), `aip/domain/brief.py`, `aip/domain/plan.py`, `aip/api/schemas.py` (`SimpleBriefRequest.to_brief`), `aip/agents/orchestrator.py` (how generation is called and how errors and advisories surface to the API/stream). Read them before changing anything; the docstrings explain the reasoning behind each choice.\n\n## What to build\n1. **Feasibility gate before evolution.** Compute the minimum floor area each level's programme needs: per room `max(min_area(type), min_clear_width(type)^2 × sensible aspect)` plus circulation and stairs, against the buildable envelope area per level. If it does not fit, resolve it in this order and record every step in `plan.metadata[\"advisories\"]` (a list of plain-English strings) so the user is told:\n   a) move rooms to an added level when the brief's FAR and height rules allow it (bedrooms go up first, public rooms stay on the ground floor, a staircase is added);\n   b) drop optional rooms in this order: study, balcony, utility, puja (fold it into an alcove note), extra bathrooms beyond one per two bedrooms plus one common;\n   c) shrink every room toward its minimum;\n   d) if it still cannot fit, raise a typed `InfeasibleBriefError` carrying a message like \"A 5-bedroom single-storey house needs about 118 m² but this plot's buildable area is 72 m². Add a floor, reduce bedrooms, or use a larger plot.\" Make sure the orchestrator and the SSE design stream turn that into a clean, visible error event, not a crash.\n   Make sure advisories reach the API response (plan metadata survives into `DesignResponse.plan`).\n2. **Stairs stack exactly.** Decide the staircase rectangle once, on the ground floor (or before evolution: a standard dog-leg about 2.4–2.7 m by 4.0–4.6 m, against a wall, adjacent to circulation), and make it a *fixed* leaf at the identical rectangle on every level. Recommended: carve it with locked prefix splits at the top of every level's slicing tree (mark those `Split`s locked so `mutate`/`crossover` never alter them), so each floor's GA only evolves the remaining region. Upper-floor lobby/corridor must touch the staircase (walkability already requires upper floors to be entered from the stair).\n3. **Room proportions.** In the surrogate and exact fitness, penalise habitable rooms past 1.6:1 steeply, and add a hard penalty past 2.2:1 for bedrooms and dining and past 2.5:1 for living, so slots never win when a better partition exists. Kitchens may go to 2.4:1 (galley). Bathrooms and utilities have minimum clear widths (bath 1.5 m, WC 1.0 m, utility 1.2 m) and a maximum of 3:1.\n4. **Less corridor.** Target corridor + lobby ≤ 10% of the floor, with a smooth penalty above it, and prefer a single short spine that every door opens off. Do not create a corridor at all when foyer + living can distribute to every room legally.\n5. Keep everything the generator already does well: zoning front to back from the road, Vastu orientation terms, walkability guardrail, deterministic seeds, and the clean-over-flawed preference in `generate`.\n\n## Acceptance (iterate until met)\n- `python -m scripts.plan_sweep --n 30`: at least **24/30 clean**, `stairs_misaligned` 0, no guardrail \"is 1.x m wide\" or \"passes through\" on any plan that was not explicitly reported infeasible (an infeasible brief that raises the typed error counts as handled, not as a defect; make the sweep catch `InfeasibleBriefError` and count it separately as \"infeasible\" and print its message).\n- Also run with `--n 60` once and report the numbers.\n- No plan takes more than 12 s to generate in the sweep (report the max).\n- Full suite passes: `.venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest -q` (275 passing now) plus `-q aip/engines/vastu/calibration/test_calibration.py`. Add tests for: stairs identical across levels, the feasibility gate's escalation (added level, dropped optional room, typed error) and its advisories, the aspect caps, and the corridor share.\n- Match the existing style: docstrings explain *why*; type hints; no new dependencies.\n\nReport back: what you changed (files and approach), the before/after sweep tables for n=30 and n=60, the max generation time, test counts, and anything you could not meet with the reason.","outputFile":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\tasks\\ac2ecc7f5007eff43.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"18e7fd72-1dda-450e-824a-42458e97f3c0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
