{"parentUuid":"12ae9298-e653-4ccd-a44a-9dacd1af4e16","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftAxiSXSdS12wSA3GhDL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Uploads are fixed: walls-only DXF and SVG files, scans and phone photos now import correctly. I re-ran the benchmark and tests myself rather than taking the agent's word. Committed locally as `f78b119`, not pushed.\n\n| File | Before | Now |\n|---|---|---|\n| Our own DXF / SVG | worked | still 12/12 rooms |\n| Walls-only DXF (typical AutoCAD output) | \"no closed room outlines\" | 12/12 rooms, all room types right, 0.1 s |\n| Walls-only SVG (Illustrator/Inkscape style) | \"no room shapes found\" | 12/12 rooms, all room types right, 0.1 s |\n| Scanned plan image | failed after 58 s on the rate-limited vision model | 12/12 rooms, all room types right, 2.3 s, no network |\n| Washed-out phone photo | failed | 12/12 rooms, all room types right, 0.9 s, no network |\n\nHere 12/12 means every room of the original plan came back in the right place. Matched rooms overlap the originals by 94–100%.\n\n- **Images are read locally:** OpenCV straightens the image and finds walls, door gaps and rooms. Local text recognition reads room names and size strings such as \"4.6 x 5.0\" or \"12000\", so the plan comes out at real scale without you entering a plot size. The free vision model is now only a fallback, capped at 20 seconds.\n- **Vector files:** rooms are rebuilt from the wall lines. SVG transforms are now applied properly, DXF unit settings are read, and door arcs and furniture blocks no longer get mistaken for walls.\n- **Tests:** all 54 import tests pass, including the 23 new ones.\n\nPlan quality is next and a fresh Sonnet agent is on it now. Today only 1 of 30 generated plans is free of the defects I measured. Its targets:\n\n- at least 24 of 30 clean\n- staircases that stack exactly between floors\n- no bedroom-through-kitchen or 1.1 m-wide rooms\n- room proportions capped so no more 3:1 bedrooms\n- corridors held to about 10% of each floor\n\nBriefs too big for the plot will be handled properly: the system adds a floor, drops optional rooms, or tells you clearly why it can't fit. I'll verify its numbers the same way when it reports back."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3132,"cache_read_input_tokens":716445,"output_tokens":786,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3132,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":786,"cache_read_input_tokens":716445,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3132,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3132},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CftAxhj73XXzd5vtvEdJ2","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"67e7d0eb-a96b-4144-bd5e-31e69cfa3e1e","timestamp":"2026-10-10T07:36:29.054Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
