{"parentUuid":"e36711fe-a06b-4df4-8629-5e352d1ec169","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftDnYXnvPgbACVwaH5fb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0198TadPMirRpcecGNcKnNT3","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"ac2ecc7f5007eff43","summary":"Wider acceptance: full multi-dimension plan audit","message":"The user asked for a multi-dimensional analysis. I wrote `scripts/plan_audit.py`, which runs 13 checks on 32 briefs, including 40×60/6-bed/4-floor and 30×40/4-bed/2-floor. On the code as committed (HEAD) the baseline is 0/32 clean. Frequencies:\n- unfurnishable 29 (e.g. a 1.4×3.9 bathroom; FURNISH minimum rectangles per type are in the script)\n- bad_proportion 23 (living 2.6:1)\n- passage_share 22\n- stairs_not_stacked 20\n- underuses_plot 15 (117 of 259 m² allowed)\n- walls_not_bearing 14 (upper-floor walls only 44% over lower walls)\n- blob_passage 12 (a corridor 2.1×4.4 m: corridors must be strips ≤ 1.8 m wide)\n- toilet_over_kitchen_puja 11 (an upper bathroom over a dining, kitchen or puja)\n- too_many_doors 7 (bedrooms with 3 doors)\n- living_far_from_dining 2, foyer_not_to_living 2, kitchen_far_from_dining 1, puja_beside_toilet 1\n\nPlease extend your work so the generator also handles:\n- corridors as true strips (width 1.0–1.5 m)\n- furniture-fit minimum dimensions per type\n- wet areas stacked vertically, never over a kitchen, dining or puja\n- upper-floor partition walls landing on lower walls or beams. Prefer aligning upper splits with lower-floor splits through the same locked-prefix idea, and target ≥ 60% of upper wall length borne.\n- bedrooms at most 2 doors (room plus attached bath)\n- foyer opening into living\n- kitchen sharing a wall with dining\n- puja never sharing a wall with a toilet\n\nNew acceptance: `python -m scripts.plan_audit --n 30` reaches **≥ 26/32 clean**, with zero stairs_not_stacked, zero toilet_over_kitchen_puja and zero underuses_plot. The plan_sweep targets still apply. Keep the 12 s per plan limit. Report the audit table before and after. Edit `scripts/plan_audit.py` only to adapt it to InfeasibleBriefError (count infeasible separately).","type":"message","recipient":"ac2ecc7f5007eff43","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"The user asked for a multi-dimensional analysis. …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1199,"cache_read_input_tokens":732478,"output_tokens":980,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":68},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1199,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":980,"cache_read_input_tokens":732478,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1199,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1199},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0198TadPMirRpcecGNcKnNT3":{"to":"ac2ecc7f5007eff43","summary":"Wider acceptance: full multi-dimension plan audit","message":"The user asked for a multi-dimensional analysis. I wrote `scripts/plan_audit.py`, which runs 13 checks on 32 briefs, including 40×60/6-bed/4-floor and 30×40/4-bed/2-floor. On the code as committed (HEAD) the baseline is 0/32 clean. Frequencies:\n- unfurnishable 29 (e.g. a 1.4×3.9 bathroom; FURNISH minimum rectangles per type are in the script)\n- bad_proportion 23 (living 2.6:1)\n- passage_share 22\n- stairs_not_stacked 20\n- underuses_plot 15 (117 of 259 m² allowed)\n- walls_not_bearing 14 (upper-floor walls only 44% over lower walls)\n- blob_passage 12 (a corridor 2.1×4.4 m: corridors must be strips ≤ 1.8 m wide)\n- toilet_over_kitchen_puja 11 (an upper bathroom over a dining, kitchen or puja)\n- too_many_doors 7 (bedrooms with 3 doors)\n- living_far_from_dining 2, foyer_not_to_living 2, kitchen_far_from_dining 1, puja_beside_toilet 1\n\nPlease extend your work so the generator also handles:\n- corridors as true strips (width 1.0–1.5 m)\n- furniture-fit minimum dimensions per type\n- wet areas stacked vertically, never over a kitchen, dining or puja\n- upper-floor partition walls landing on lower walls or beams. Prefer aligning upper splits with lower-floor splits through the same locked-prefix idea, and target ≥ 60% of upper wall length borne.\n- bedrooms at most 2 doors (room plus attached bath)\n- foyer opening into living\n- kitchen sharing a wall with dining\n- puja never sharing a wall with a toilet\n\nNew acceptance: `python -m scripts.plan_audit --n 30` reaches **≥ 26/32 clean**, with zero stairs_not_stacked, zero toilet_over_kitchen_puja and zero underuses_plot. The plan_sweep targets still apply. Keep the 12 s per plan limit. Report the audit table before and after. Edit `scripts/plan_audit.py` only to adapt it to InfeasibleBriefError (count infeasible separately)."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CftDnXpNU5jBXbpes4eyy","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"95a6a685-a2b7-450f-92c9-6bd08cf276b0","timestamp":"2026-10-10T08:13:32.858Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
