{"parentUuid":"28e8dfdc-9d1a-4931-ade9-1faf461f6189","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CftJVF5ev8niWkyQiQYLV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0188hbB913JinvbLKVP3mZrq","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://neatlogs.com/hackathon","prompt":"Extract every rule, guideline, requirement, deadline, submission format, commit/checkpoint requirement, judging criteria, allowed tools, required integrations (e.g. Neatlogs SDK), and repository requirements. Quote exact wording for rules."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":685,"cache_read_input_tokens":736517,"output_tokens":318,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":685,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":318,"cache_read_input_tokens":736517,"cache_creation_input_tokens":685,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":685},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0188hbB913JinvbLKVP3mZrq":{"url":"https://neatlogs.com/hackathon","prompt":"Extract every rule, guideline, requirement, deadline, submission format, commit/checkpoint requirement, judging criteria, allowed tools, required integrations (e.g. Neatlogs SDK), and repository requirements. Quote exact wording for rules."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CftJVEfcGzxKjEggZXj4A","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"278f6845-ddab-4549-bdd1-823ec47cb6f7","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:15:05.340Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"28e8dfdc-9d1a-4931-ade9-1faf461f6189","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cde90b88-60f3-4a8e-aba6-b51e470ae5ea","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FD9QGuSjWeyZJNzZMY6ijY","type":"tool_result","content":"## Event and Deadlines\n- **Dates:** Oct 10–11, 2026 (virtual).\n- **Submission deadline:** Not stated.\n\n## Judging and Prize\n- **Prize:** Best Use of Entire. \"Awarded to the team whose project makes the most creative use of Checkpoints, Graph or Brain.\"\n- **Other criteria:** None listed. The page says \"Feel free to be creative and impress!\" for the \"Other\" idea category.\n\n## Submission Requirements\nThe page offers a \"suggested\" checklist, so these are recommendations rather than mandatory rules:\n- **Project:** Name and short explanation of what you built.\n- **Entire usage:** Which features you used and how they support the project.\n- **Demo:** A working link or short recording of the main workflow.\n- **Repository:** Source code with setup and run instructions.\n- **Checkpoint:** An accessible Entire checkpoint link and its checkpoint ID.\n\n## Checkpoint Requirements\n- \"A normal committed checkpoint needs both captured agent context and a Git commit.\"\n- Push your branch, then run `entire status` to verify checkpoint sync.\n- Share the link format `https://entire.io/gh/OWNER/REPO/commit/FULL_COMMIT_SHA` for GitHub-backed repos.\n- Open repository → branch → commit → checkpoint, then show **Sessions** (request and decisions) and **Changes** (implementation).\n- Access: \"Make sure reviewers have access. A URL does not grant permissions,\" and \"checkpoints stored in public repositories are public.\"\n- When committing, choose **yes** if prompted to link the commit to session context.\n\n## Repository and Access Requirements\n- Every team member signs in to Entire with GitHub and authorizes the Entire GitHub App.\n- A GitHub organization admin installs the app and imports the repository. Until then, the repo doesn't appear for the team.\n- Changes can take up to an hour to sync.\n- Access follows the GitHub collaborator list, so roles match GitHub roles.\n\n## Optional Tracks\n- **Trails:** Optional. Requires requesting access via the form and an admin enabling Runners, Auto build on push, and Trails in repo settings. \"Each Trail is currently backed by a GitHub PR for CI.\"\n- **Continuous Memory (Graph/Brain):** Optional, only needed if building with Entire Graph or Brain.\n\n## Tools and Integrations\n- The page names no restricted or allowed tool list.\n- It supports multiple coding agents (e.g., Claude Code, Codex) and allows new ones via the Agent Integration Protocol.\n\n## Not Specified\n- Submission deadline and submission method\n- Team size limits\n- Judging process or criteria beyond the single prize description\n- Allowed tools or languages"}]},"uuid":"22e2671c-f5b1-4580-9b48-69a6fc47b16e","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:15:12.573Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":31919,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"## Event and Deadlines\n- **Dates:** Oct 10–11, 2026 (virtual).\n- **Submission deadline:** Not stated.\n\n## Judging and Prize\n- **Prize:** Best Use of Entire. \"Awarded to the team whose project makes the most creative use of Checkpoints, Graph or Brain.\"\n- **Other criteria:** None listed. The page says \"Feel free to be creative and impress!\" for the \"Other\" idea category.\n\n## Submission Requirements\nThe page offers a \"suggested\" checklist, so these are recommendations rather than mandatory rules:\n- **Project:** Name and short explanation of what you built.\n- **Entire usage:** Which features you used and how they support the project.\n- **Demo:** A working link or short recording of the main workflow.\n- **Repository:** Source code with setup and run instructions.\n- **Checkpoint:** An accessible Entire checkpoint link and its checkpoint ID.\n\n## Checkpoint Requirements\n- \"A normal committed checkpoint needs both captured agent context and a Git commit.\"\n- Push your branch, then run `entire status` to verify checkpoint sync.\n- Share the link format `https://entire.io/gh/OWNER/REPO/commit/FULL_COMMIT_SHA` for GitHub-backed repos.\n- Open repository → branch → commit → checkpoint, then show **Sessions** (request and decisions) and **Changes** (implementation).\n- Access: \"Make sure reviewers have access. A URL does not grant permissions,\" and \"checkpoints stored in public repositories are public.\"\n- When committing, choose **yes** if prompted to link the commit to session context.\n\n## Repository and Access Requirements\n- Every team member signs in to Entire with GitHub and authorizes the Entire GitHub App.\n- A GitHub organization admin installs the app and imports the repository. Until then, the repo doesn't appear for the team.\n- Changes can take up to an hour to sync.\n- Access follows the GitHub collaborator list, so roles match GitHub roles.\n\n## Optional Tracks\n- **Trails:** Optional. Requires requesting access via the form and an admin enabling Runners, Auto build on push, and Trails in repo settings. \"Each Trail is currently backed by a GitHub PR for CI.\"\n- **Continuous Memory (Graph/Brain):** Optional, only needed if building with Entire Graph or Brain.\n\n## Tools and Integrations\n- The page names no restricted or allowed tool list.\n- It supports multiple coding agents (e.g., Claude Code, Codex) and allows new ones via the Agent Integration Protocol.\n\n## Not Specified\n- Submission deadline and submission method\n- Team size limits\n- Judging process or criteria beyond the single prize description\n- Allowed tools or languages","durationMs":8206,"url":"https://hack.entire.io/neathacks-2026/"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"28e8dfdc-9d1a-4931-ade9-1faf461f6189","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"278f6845-ddab-4549-bdd1-823ec47cb6f7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cde90b88-60f3-4a8e-aba6-b51e470ae5ea","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0188hbB913JinvbLKVP3mZrq","type":"tool_result","content":"# neatHack Rules and Requirements\n\n## Dates and Deadlines (IST)\n- **Kickoff call:** Oct 10, 9:00 AM. The page says it includes a workshop with TheVibeFounder, Q&A, and introductions to judges and mentors.\n- **Hackathon begins:** Oct 10, 12:30 PM. AWS and CrustData credits are transferred at this time.\n- **Final workshops:** Sun, Oct 11, the last round of technical support before submissions.\n- **Submission:** Mon, Oct 12, 7:00–11:55 PM. The page says submissions are \"opening soon.\"\n- **Winners announced:** Oct 16.\n- Team check-in is through the web check-in page.\n\n## Track\n- One track. \"Build an AI agent, or a team of agents, that completes a substantial task from start to finish.\"\n- Focus areas: planning, tool use, state, context, execution, recovery, verification, and iteration.\n- Example tasks are illustrative, and you don't have to build one of them.\n\n## Required Integrations\n- \"Your project must use neatlogs, Entire and cfo.ai.\"\n- Use neatlogs and Entire to build and improve the agent. Use cfo.ai to plan the business.\n- Include the resulting cfo.ai business plan in your submission, covering pricing, costs, revenue, and runway.\n- cfo.ai signup requires a card. \"Immediately after signing up, cancel your subscription in Settings → Billing.\" The neatHack team provides the credits directly.\n\n## Submission Requirements\n- Submit on X by quoting the official neatlogs post with your team, name, project, public repo, and demo.\n- neatlogs and cfo.ai will engage with the first 50 quote tweets.\n\n## Required Evidence\n- **Improvement:** A before-and-after run comparison, such as two neatlogs traces with the numbers compared.\n- **neatlogs use:** Links to traces from your project, or screenshots.\n- **Entire use:** Checkpoints or entire-graph output from your repository.\n- **cfo.ai use:** A business plan covering pricing, costs, revenue, and runway.\n- **Failure recovery:** A run where an action failed, showing what the agent did next.\n- **Building in public:** Links to what you shared during the hackathon, tagged #neatHack.\n- **Original work:** A public repository with commits dated during the hackathon.\n\n## Repository Requirements\n- A public repository.\n- Commits dated during the hackathon.\n- Entire checkpoints or entire-graph output from the repository.\n\n## Judging Criteria (each scored out of 100)\n- **The agent (30%):** Handles a substantial task from start to finish.\n- **Use of neatlogs, Entire, and cfo.ai (25%):** Used to build, improve, and plan a business around the agent.\n- **Demo video (20%):** Clearly explains the agent and the use of the three tools.\n- **Building in public (15%):** Sharing the project during the build.\n- **Usefulness and originality (10%):** Solves a real problem in a new way.\n\n## Prizes\n- **1st:** $2,000 cash + $5,000 Dodo Payments credits\n- **2nd:** $1,000 cash + $3,000 Dodo Payments credits\n- **3rd:** $500 cash + $1,000 Dodo Payments credits\n- **Each placed winner:** 3 months of neatlogs Pro (worth $1,500)\n- **Community winner:** $500 cash, for community impact. It can be won alongside a top-three placement.\n\n## Credits and Resources\n- **AWS:** One $25 allowance per team or solo, for the first 350 teams to complete web check-in. Covers EC2, Lambda, IAM roles, and load balancers in us-east-1. Bedrock is not included. Model API calls use your own OpenAI or Anthropic keys, billed separately.\n- **Crustdata:** 5,000 credits for every participant.\n\n## Not Specified on the Page\n- The answers to the FAQs on team size, pre-event work, conduct rules, and help/credits are not included in the text. Only the questions appear.\n- Team size limits, allowed tools beyond the required integrations, and conduct rules are not stated."}]},"uuid":"57a3d6d3-b210-49af-8ef1-830ebdaeba2f","timestamp":"2026-10-10T09:15:17.243Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":276599,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# neatHack Rules and Requirements\n\n## Dates and Deadlines (IST)\n- **Kickoff call:** Oct 10, 9:00 AM. The page says it includes a workshop with TheVibeFounder, Q&A, and introductions to judges and mentors.\n- **Hackathon begins:** Oct 10, 12:30 PM. AWS and CrustData credits are transferred at this time.\n- **Final workshops:** Sun, Oct 11, the last round of technical support before submissions.\n- **Submission:** Mon, Oct 12, 7:00–11:55 PM. The page says submissions are \"opening soon.\"\n- **Winners announced:** Oct 16.\n- Team check-in is through the web check-in page.\n\n## Track\n- One track. \"Build an AI agent, or a team of agents, that completes a substantial task from start to finish.\"\n- Focus areas: planning, tool use, state, context, execution, recovery, verification, and iteration.\n- Example tasks are illustrative, and you don't have to build one of them.\n\n## Required Integrations\n- \"Your project must use neatlogs, Entire and cfo.ai.\"\n- Use neatlogs and Entire to build and improve the agent. Use cfo.ai to plan the business.\n- Include the resulting cfo.ai business plan in your submission, covering pricing, costs, revenue, and runway.\n- cfo.ai signup requires a card. \"Immediately after signing up, cancel your subscription in Settings → Billing.\" The neatHack team provides the credits directly.\n\n## Submission Requirements\n- Submit on X by quoting the official neatlogs post with your team, name, project, public repo, and demo.\n- neatlogs and cfo.ai will engage with the first 50 quote tweets.\n\n## Required Evidence\n- **Improvement:** A before-and-after run comparison, such as two neatlogs traces with the numbers compared.\n- **neatlogs use:** Links to traces from your project, or screenshots.\n- **Entire use:** Checkpoints or entire-graph output from your repository.\n- **cfo.ai use:** A business plan covering pricing, costs, revenue, and runway.\n- **Failure recovery:** A run where an action failed, showing what the agent did next.\n- **Building in public:** Links to what you shared during the hackathon, tagged #neatHack.\n- **Original work:** A public repository with commits dated during the hackathon.\n\n## Repository Requirements\n- A public repository.\n- Commits dated during the hackathon.\n- Entire checkpoints or entire-graph output from the repository.\n\n## Judging Criteria (each scored out of 100)\n- **The agent (30%):** Handles a substantial task from start to finish.\n- **Use of neatlogs, Entire, and cfo.ai (25%):** Used to build, improve, and plan a business around the agent.\n- **Demo video (20%):** Clearly explains the agent and the use of the three tools.\n- **Building in public (15%):** Sharing the project during the build.\n- **Usefulness and originality (10%):** Solves a real problem in a new way.\n\n## Prizes\n- **1st:** $2,000 cash + $5,000 Dodo Payments credits\n- **2nd:** $1,000 cash + $3,000 Dodo Payments credits\n- **3rd:** $500 cash + $1,000 Dodo Payments credits\n- **Each placed winner:** 3 months of neatlogs Pro (worth $1,500)\n- **Community winner:** $500 cash, for community impact. It can be won alongside a top-three placement.\n\n## Credits and Resources\n- **AWS:** One $25 allowance per team or solo, for the first 350 teams to complete web check-in. Covers EC2, Lambda, IAM roles, and load balancers in us-east-1. Bedrock is not included. Model API calls use your own OpenAI or Anthropic keys, billed separately.\n- **Crustdata:** 5,000 credits for every participant.\n\n## Not Specified on the Page\n- The answers to the FAQs on team size, pre-event work, conduct rules, and help/credits are not included in the text. Only the questions appear.\n- Team size limits, allowed tools beyond the required integrations, and conduct rules are not stated.","durationMs":11887,"url":"https://neatlogs.com/hackathon"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"278f6845-ddab-4549-bdd1-823ec47cb6f7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
