{"parentUuid":"46b1acb2-944d-4516-b3ca-4b4fc93a7b65","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14999637 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4792ad89-c4f8-460b-8a30-898807d75f77","timestamp":"2026-10-10T13:28:13.955Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14999637 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"4792ad89-c4f8-460b-8a30-898807d75f77","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cftdo7Mne4VhxEWdPJHrt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"It's because the agent rebuilt most of the generator: almost all of the new code is new subsystems, not bloat. The function names show where it went:\n\n- **Stairs:** `StairPlan`, `carve_stair` and `_plan_stairs` place one staircase and lock it in the same spot on every floor.\n- **Feasibility and plot fit:** `_resolve_programme`, `_grow_programme`, `_design_footprint` and `_footprint_cap` decide whether a brief fits the plot. They grow small houses to fill big plots, and they shrink or drop rooms, or add a floor, when a brief doesn't fit.\n- **New layout seeding:** `build_banded_tree`, `_row_tree`, `_deal` and `_seed_population` lay rooms out in rows from the road back, instead of random slicing.\n- **Defect checks and repair:** `_Assessment`, `_judge`, `_repair`, `_household_problems` and `_findings` check each audit rule (proportions, corridors, wet stacking, adjacency) and fix violations.\n- **Structure and scoring:** `_borne_ratio` keeps upper-floor walls over lower ones, and `proportion_penalty`, `corridor_penalty` and `_surrogate_relations` steer the search toward good plans.\n\nMy one concern is size: layout.py has roughly doubled. When the agent finishes I'll judge it on the measured audit and sweep results, and on whether the code is clean enough to maintain, not on line count. If it's bloated, I'll have it trimmed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":726,"cache_read_input_tokens":750735,"output_tokens":509,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":726,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"