{"parentUuid":"30debcde-ede5-4d2e-a959-19d1b9dd9f67","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cde90b88-60f3-4a8e-aba6-b51e470ae5ea","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - **Project:** Atri Arch / Architect Intelligence Platform (FastAPI backend in `backend/`, static frontend in `frontend/`).\n   - **Ground rules:**\n     - Production-grade quality.\n     - Reply in chained one-line updates.\n     - Minimise tokens.\n     - Never git push unless asked.\n     - No subagents unless asked.\n     - Credentials only in the gitignored `.env`; never commit credentials.\n     - Don't fabricate commits.\n   - **Requests in this session** (each \"do one by one\", fastest to slowest, homepage last):\n     - **Plan quality:** fix plans of all sizes, small included. Evaluate across many dimensions and keep text-to-plan compatible.\n     - **Programme honesty:** user-requested rooms must always be included (courtyard, balcony, study, etc.) and nothing unrequested added.\n     - **Workers:** scale the miniature workers to plot size. Randomize their work every render, but no random asymmetric lines; make it look like real work.\n     - **Loading pacing:** slow down after the plan is built, with critiques and conversations continuing. Add a fast-forward button bottom right.\n     - **Fit-out animation:** plants growing naturally, furniture placed, walls painted.\n     - **3D:**\n       - Colour palettes recommended by AI, with next-palette and text colour preferences; minimized palette card.\n       - Fix wall glitching.\n       - Fix furniture facing walls.\n       - Many unique exterior designs based on user preferences, made by a specialised exterior agent. Remove the green wall.\n     - **Vastu 3D:** better visualization, no balls, text readable.\n     - **Drawings:** make elevations, sections, roof and site interactive and dynamic.\n     - **Text-to-plan as an agentic chat:**\n       - Must understand anything, any language.\n       - Asks follow-ups and auto-starts on confirmation.\n       - Production-grade chat UI that doesn't look AI-made.\n       - Typewriter examples instead of cards; no \"Enter to send\" hint.\n       - Boxy, sharp buttons.\n       - Drag-and-drop or attach a plan in the chat instead of \"Review my plan\".\n       - The manual form stays as a drawer.\n     - **Edit after creation:** revise via text.\n     - **Degraded critiques:** fix the \"degraded mode\" error. The user supplied API keys.\n     - **Header:** remove \"ENGINE READY\"; wordmark ATRI (bold) ARCH (light, sand); new gold lattice-arch logo.\n     - **Homepage:** the best UI possible, dynamic, explains everything, hackathon (NeatHacks) ready.\n     - **Interior tab:** dynamic, with furniture and interior designs.\n   - **Latest instruction:** \"yeah start working on each one by one\", meaning the remaining checklist.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **Spine planner (`spine.py`):**\n     - A hall spine with two stacks of rows: suites, side-by-side pairs, smalls packed.\n     - Variants: public_left, stair_at, bath_behind, wide, transverse, single-loaded.\n     - `_fit_level`: move suites across the hall, drop optional extras (never \"Requested\"), shrink to max(scale, 85% of asked).\n     - Garden L-shapes propagate to upper floors.\n     - Hall trimmed to the last door it serves; foyer across hall plus the private-stack front.\n     - Stair spans the full stack width, 3.81 m run.\n     - Toilet-over-kitchen quality penalty; balcony attach_to host.\n   - **LayoutGenerator integration:**\n     - `_spine_candidates()` runs before the GA; the GA is skipped if there are enough guardrail-clean plans.\n     - `_open_outline` flag: single-room walls count as exterior.\n     - `_doors_to_hosts`; `config.spine`; `auto_extras`; requested-rooms guardrail.\n   - **Brief agent (`brief_agent.py`):**\n     - Rule parser plus LLM `llm_turn` with CHAT_SYSTEM: any language, JSON reply/updates/questions/go_ahead/start.\n     - `_clean` validation; the model may only fill blanks.\n     - START regex; `to_request`; `revise` via LLM with rules as fallback.\n   - **LLM router:**\n     - Key rotation via `ProviderSpec.credentials()` (comma-separated), `KEYS_PER_PROVIDER` limiter scaling.\n     - Retry rounds with backoff; 429s don't open the breaker.\n   - **3D (`arch3d.py`):**\n     - PBR via trimesh; sRGB→linear conversion; two-leaf walls with per-room finishes.\n     - `_merged_walls` dedupe; palettes (12 schemes).\n     - Exterior grammar (`exteriors.py`): design id `ex:roof.base.upper.screen.windows.p|n.accent`; skins as wall material.\n     - Roofs: flat / slab / mono(pitch) / butterfly / hip / gable.\n   - **Viewer3D:** `setMode`, `setVastu`, `setOrtho` (elevations, sections with clipping), `setSun`, datums, `focusRoom`, `load(url, {keepView, front})`.\n   - **Atelier (`stage3d.js`):** playbooks, `_sizeFig`, fit-out (paint, furniture, garden), `calm`/`hurry`/`idle`, fast-forward.\n   - **Frontend:** `home.js` chat; `home-hero.js` live building hero plus airflow showcase; demo assets in `frontend/demo/`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`backend/aip/engines/architecture/spine.py` (new, core):**\n     - SpinePlanner(envelope, road, stair_on, outer=site_box).\n     - Variant dataclass (public_left, stair_at, bath_behind, wide, transverse, single, ell); `_rows`, `plan`, `_fit_level`, `_fill`, `_trim_hall`.\n     - Constants: SPINE=1.3, FOYER=1.9, GROW=1.1, STAIR_L=4.6 (stair_len 3.81).\n     - The latest uncommitted edit (upper-floor split) prefers suites on the private side:\n       ```python\n       for it in sorted(priv, key=lambda i: (i.bath is None, -(i.area + (i.bath.area if i.bath else 0)))):\n           d = it.area / 4 + (BATH_DEPTH if it.bath else 0)\n           if (it.bath is not None and dq <= dp + 3.0) or (it.bath is None and dp > dq + 3.0):\n               priv2.append(it); dq += d\n           elif dp <= dq or it.bath is None:\n               pub.append(it); dp += d\n           else:\n               priv2.append(it); dq += d\n       ```\n   - **`backend/aip/engines/architecture/layout.py`:**\n     - `_spine_candidates`, `_doors_to_hosts`, `_open_outline` in `_build_walls`, toilet-over penalty.\n     - Requested-missing guardrail; requested rooms dropped last in the feasibility gate; `auto_extras` gating of EXTRA_ROOMS.\n     - `GeneratorConfig.spine`.\n   - **`backend/aip/api/schemas.py`:**\n     - RoomRequest gains level/scale/attach_to.\n     - SimpleBriefRequest gains extra_rooms/remove_rooms/auto_extras; `_apply_extras`; named amenities marked \"Requested by the client.\".\n     - Dining and utility are default unless \"no dining\"/\"no utility\".\n   - **`backend/aip/agents/brief_agent.py`:** parse, llm_turn, _clean, converse (returns start flag), revise (LLM first), to_request, START regex.\n   - **`backend/aip/agents/exterior_agent.py`:** `design_exteriors(plan, preferences)` returns 8 LLM designs plus grammar fill to 10, cached.\n   - **`backend/aip/engines/experience/exteriors.py`:** grammar, generate, apply, skins, roof.\n   - **`backend/aip/engines/experience/facades.py`:**\n     - Legacy designs (garden removed); `edges`, `pitch_roof`.\n   - **`backend/aip/engines/experience/arch3d.py`:**\n     - Ex materials; skins; roof dispatch; `_flat_roof_extras`.\n     - `_linear` conversion; `_merged_walls`; the furniture lz sign fix.\n   - **`backend/aip/engines/experience/palettes.py`:** schemes, preferences_from_text, rank, resolve.\n   - **`backend/aip/engines/architecture/windflow.py`:** whole-floor airflow solve; from the earlier session, committed.\n   - **`backend/aip/engines/vastu/placements.py`:** grid-cell judging, swap logic.\n   - **`backend/aip/api/routers/`:**\n     - `plans.py`: `/airflow/{level}`, `/palettes` (with designs), `/exteriors`, `/vastu3d`; `model.glb` takes palette/colours/design.\n     - `design.py`: `/design/chat` (history), `/design/revise`.\n   - **`backend/aip/core/`:**\n     - `providers.py`: `_ROTATION` and credentials rotation.\n     - `llm.py`: retry rounds, KEYS_PER_PROVIDER, 429 handling.\n   - **`frontend/`:**\n     - `home.js`: chat with brief strip, typewriter ghost examples, attach/drag-drop via `uploadFile`, auto-start.\n     - `home-hero.js`: hero build animation over `demo/house0-2.glb`; airflow tile from `demo/air.json`.\n     - `studio.js`:\n       - `initHome`, setField, openManual.\n       - Facade selector from `/exteriors`; renderInterior rewrite; loadOrthoSheet; renderAir.\n       - Revise box; paletteCard; phase fallback.\n     - `viewer3d.js`: focusRoom, setOrtho, setVastu, palette reloads.\n     - `stage3d.js` and `atelier.js`: playbooks, fit-out, showtime, fast-forward.\n     - `index.html`:\n       - Chat div, sheet drawer, hero3d, explain/show/board/cta sections.\n       - Wordmark `<span>Atri<b>Arch</b></span>`; logo `logo-arch.svg`.\n     - `rabbit.css`: many appended blocks.\n   - **`.claude/launch.json`:** added \"aip-dev\" (port 8001).\n   - **`.env` (gitignored):** `GROQ_API_KEY=<key1>,<key2>` and `GOOGLE_API_KEY`. Never commit or echo these.\n   - **`backend/scripts/plan_audit.py`:** passage share 0.15; stair FURNISH (2.3, 3.3) and >14 m² oversize.\n   - **Tests:**\n     - `backend/tests/test_feasibility.py`: `_brief` sets auto_extras=True; optional-order test updated.\n     - `backend/tests/test_import.py` and `scripts/import_fixtures.py`: use `spine=False`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Backslash mangling in bash heredocs:** patches written via Write-tool .py files or `chr(92)`.\n   - **`_fit` name clash:** renamed to `_sizeFig`.\n   - **Hall label broke importer and tests:** renamed to Corridor/Family.\n   - **Degraded critiques:** were rate limits. Fixed with key rotation plus retry rounds plus no breaker on 429; 30 parallel calls verified 0 offline.\n   - **Chat HTTP 405:** the old server was on port 8000; killed PID 24456 and started the \"aip\" preview.\n   - **LLM re-guessing the plot on \"G+1\":** model limited to filling blanks.\n   - **Interior black stage:** polygons are `[x, y]` arrays; fixed with `q.x ?? q[0]`. Framing scaled by fov and aspect.\n   - **Upper floor overhanging the garden:** garden recorded per stack and applied above.\n   - **Puja beside toilet:** store spacer row inserted.\n   - **View-transition hang:** 1.5 s fallback applies the phase.\n   - **User feedback applied:**\n     - One-line updates.\n     - Garden \"too forced\" changed to natural sparse growth.\n     - No random diagonal lines.\n     - Palette card minimized.\n     - Remove green wall.\n     - Chat looked AI-made, so redesigned.\n     - Engine-ready text removed.\n     - Buttons boxy.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Spine sweep** (32 briefs via `scratchpad/sp2.py`):\n     - Guardrail failures about 0.\n     - \"none\" (no spine fit) 12, which fall back to the GA.\n     - Remaining audit flags: underuses_plot 11 (by design: garden), toilet_over_kitchen_puja 8–9, plate_fill 5.\n   - **Full tests:** about 6–7 failures, mostly pre-existing.\n   - **Homepage, chat, exteriors and interiors** verified in the browser (pane screenshots are limited at narrow width).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"what else is left?, run the project\"\n   - Screenshot of a bad plan, then: \"start working on the other parts of the project, and i hope the plan quality improves, cause even right now it doesnt make sense\"\n   - \"the 3d models it generated, let it be colour filled with the colour palette that the ai recommends too, but properly and where needed, with a next colour palette option there too to see the options that match the exterior and interiors too, and that text to project configuration too when the user gives their colour preferences too\"\n   - \"reply in chained messages, one line updates, dont make me keep remining you\"\n   - \"when the minifigurines are designing this plan while its loading, add in more animations and dynamics like plants growing around, furniture being placed, walls being painted and many more features you think are good\"\n   - \"see these plans, theres so many issues\" (screenshots)\n   - \"keep this minimized\" (palette card screenshot)\n   - \"the colour palettes arent loading in the daytime model and theres some glitching going on in the walls in the ground flloor, fix them\"\n   - \"nah theres too much environment, kind of forced, make it natural, it has to be like its growing out when the timelapse is happening\"\n   - Long checklist message:\n     - big plots give bad designs; check the agent's efficiency and cancel it if it doesn't make sense\n     - resize workers to plot size\n     - text-to-plan agentic chat with follow-ups, manual mode as a side option, dynamic plans (attached image)\n     - homepage best UI, hackathon-ready for neathacks\n     - change logo (attached)\n     - workers do different moves every render\n     - elevations/sections/roof/site interactive\n     - many unique interior/exterior designs; fix furniture facing walls\n     - vastu 3D renders bad\n     - edit plans after creation via text\n     - do these fastest to slowest, UI last, least tokens\n   - Images: logo and reference floor plan.\n   - \"chained messages, one line updates, told you a hundred times\"\n   - \"fix this too, if you need new api keys here you go: [two Groq keys and one Google key]\". Security: these keys must stay only in `.env`, never committed or echoed.\n   - \"do everything you can to utilize the least amount of tokens while not compromising on quality, chained messages, one sentence updates only when needed\" (repeated several times)\n   - \"ok look i told you to make them randomized, but dont make then draw assymetric lines randomly across the board, let it look like they're actually doing work but unique every single time, and slow down a bit when the critiques and conversations are happening to show what the ai agents are doing in the backend\"\n   - \"fix small plans too, see all kinds of plans made by different dimensions and evaluate them based on correctness, keep it compatible for text to plan implementation too\"\n   - \"see the user can add or not add in rooms like courtyards/ balconies/ study rooms or anything like that, make sure everything is accounted for, also the loading with miniature people, i have an idea... slow things down (not too slow) after the plan is being built and evaluated, conversations, all that, even if the actual plans have loaded in, but add a fast forward button in the bottom right (with good animation) that then speeds up things even more and finishes that work they do\"\n   - \"whats this green thing on the wall bruh, remove that\"\n   - Screenshots, then: \"why is this error still appearing, fix it / remove that engine ready text, looks bad / the chat UI looks AI made, make it look like a production grade chat... has to be really intelligent and has to literally understand anything, any language, anything / the text ATRI ARCH next to the logo looks plain, change it to look like this image\"\n   - \"Try again\" plus screenshot of the chat not auto-starting: \"fix this issue too, it doesnt start automatically. Also exteriors are still the default designs, I need many many exterior designs, each unique and stylish, based on the users preferences, design some really good exteriors, keep one agent just for that and specialize it in exteriors\"\n   - \"I hit my usage limit while you were working, but it has reset now. Please continue from where you left off.\"\n   - \"what else is left out of my checklist\"\n   - Screenshots, then: \"yeah start working on each one by one / fix the chat issue, remove this line 'Enter to send...', instead of those predefined cards, make it dynamic like some chatbots where it types out one example, backspaces fast and types out another... dont make the buttons too round, keep them a little boxy and sharp... the review my plan feature can just be a drag and drop into chat or add media in the text box instead, the form / for the homepage i need the best UI possible with all the skills necessary / do everything you can to utilize the least amount of tokens...\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Remaining checklist items, one by one:\n     - Toilets over kitchen/dining upstairs (in progress).\n     - Small/tight plots where the spine planner can't fit; the GA fallback is weak.\n     - The board is sometimes empty at \"Decided\".\n     - Pre-existing failing import tests.\n     - `test_other_briefs_walk_through[kw1]`.\n   - Further homepage polish if wanted.\n   - Commit the current uncommitted spine change once verified.\n   - Never push unless asked.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   - Working on the remaining checklist \"one by one\". The last item was upstairs toilets landing over the ground-floor kitchen.\n   - I edited the upper-floor split in `backend/aip/engines/architecture/spine.py` so suites (bedrooms with baths) prefer the private side (code above) and rooms without baths go over the kitchen side.\n   - The sweep after this edit (`scratchpad/sp2.py`) showed:\n     ```\n     none 12 clean 0\n     toilet_over_kitchen_puja 9, underuses_plot 11, plate_fill 5, passage_share 4 ...\n     ```\n   - So the change did not reduce toilet_over_kitchen (9) and slightly increased \"none\" (11 to 12). The edit is uncommitted.\n   - Last commit: `944b006 feat(plans): L-shaped houses, a trimmed hall, no puja beside a toilet`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   - The edit didn't help, so decide whether to revert it or improve it. One option is to align upper-floor bath rows over ground-floor wet rows, the stair or the living room, by checking ground-floor kitchen and dining canonical rects when ordering upper rows.\n   - Then re-run the sweep and tests and commit.\n   - This continues the user's instruction \"yeah start working on each one by one\", picking up from the toilet-over-kitchen issue just tested.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\shrey\\.claude\\projects\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"7b2d4ec1-0525-4f44-993e-d6f5b9282371","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:55:36.391Z","turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["297a543f-a6f3-40d9-a884-476407ac5284"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"7b2d4ec1-0525-4f44-993e-d6f5b9282371","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\scratchpad\\focus.js","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\scratchpad\\focus.js","content":"\n  // Stand in a room: cut the house open at its floor, put the camera in a\n  // corner at eye height and look across to the far side.\n  focusRoom(box, level = 0, instant = false) {\n    if (!this.model) return;\n    this.setMode(\"interior\", level);\n    let base = 0;\n    const g = this.model.getObjectByName(`level_${level}`);\n    if (g) {\n      const bb = new THREE.Box3().setFromObject(g);\n      if (!bb.isEmpty()) base = bb.min.y;\n    }\n    const local = (x, y, h) => this.model.localToWorld(new THREE.Vector3(x, h, -y));\n    const cx = (box.x0 + box.x1) / 2, cy = (box.y0 + box.y1) / 2;\n    const w = box.x1 - box.x0, d = box.y1 - box.y0;\n    const floorY = base - this.model.position.y + 0.45;\n    // From above and outside the room's corner, looking down into it: a doll's-house view.\n    const eye = local(box.x0 - w * 0.15, box.y0 - d * 0.15, floorY + Math.max(w, d) * 1.1 + 1.6);\n    const at = local(cx, cy, floorY + 0.4);\n    this.controls.autoRotate = false;\n    if (instant) {\n      this.camera.position.copy(eye); this.controls.target.copy(at); this.controls.update();\n      return;\n    }\n    const from = this.camera.position.clone(), t0 = this.controls.target.clone();\n    const start = performance.now();\n    const step = (now) => {\n      const k = Math.min(1, (now - start) / 1000), e = 1 - Math.pow(1 - k, 3);\n      this.camera.position.lerpVectors(from, eye, e);\n      this.controls.target.lerpVectors(t0, at, e);\n      if (k < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step);\n    };\n    requestAnimationFrame(step);\n  }\n","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":35}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\..\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\scratchpad\\focus.js"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"32fb1943-a944-4ee7-9dbf-1a5b49f010e6","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:55:37.014Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"F:\\\\Users\\\\shrey\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\\\scratchpad\\\\focus.js\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\n2\t  // Stand in a room: cut the house open at its floor, put the camera in a\n3\t  // corner at eye height and look across to the far side.\n4\t  focusRoom(box, level = 0, instant = false) {\n5\t    if (!this.model) return;\n6\t    this.setMode(\"interior\", level);\n7\t    let base = 0;\n8\t    const g = this.model.getObjectByName(`level_${level}`);\n9\t    if (g) {\n10\t      const bb = new THREE.Box3().setFromObject(g);\n11\t      if (!bb.isEmpty()) base = bb.min.y;\n12\t    }\n13\t    const local = (x, y, h) => this.model.localToWorld(new THREE.Vector3(x, h, -y));\n14\t    const cx = (box.x0 + box.x1) / 2, cy = (box.y0 + box.y1) / 2;\n15\t    const w = box.x1 - box.x0, d = box.y1 - box.y0;\n16\t    const floorY = base - this.model.position.y + 0.45;\n17\t    // From above and outside the room's corner, looking down into it: a doll's-house view.\n18\t    const eye = local(box.x0 - w * 0.15, box.y0 - d * 0.15, floorY + Math.max(w, d) * 1.1 + 1.6);\n19\t    const at = local(cx, cy, floorY + 0.4);\n20\t    this.controls.autoRotate = false;\n21\t    if (instant) {\n22\t      this.camera.position.copy(eye); this.controls.target.copy(at); this.controls.update();\n23\t      return;\n24\t    }\n25\t    const from = this.camera.position.clone(), t0 = this.controls.target.clone();\n26\t    const start = performance.now();\n27\t    const step = (now) => {\n28\t      const k = Math.min(1, (now - start) / 1000), e = 1 - Math.pow(1 - k, 3);\n29\t      this.camera.position.lerpVectors(from, eye, e);\n30\t      this.controls.target.lerpVectors(t0, at, e);\n31\t      if (k < 1) requestAnimationFrame(step);\n32\t    };\n33\t    requestAnimationFrame(step);\n34\t  }\n35\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"32fb1943-a944-4ee7-9dbf-1a5b49f010e6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\scratchpad\\interior.js","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\scratchpad\\interior.js","content":"async function renderInterior() {\n  const p = pane(\"interior\");\n  p.innerHTML = \"\";\n  const id = S.activeId;\n  const plan = cur().plan;\n  const wrap = el(\"div\", \"inx\");\n  const side = el(\"aside\", \"inx__side\");\n  const stage = el(\"div\", \"inx__stage model-stage\");\n  const info = el(\"div\", \"inx__info\");\n  wrap.append(side, stage);\n  p.append(wrap);\n\n  // The interior scheme (furniture, finishes, costs), solved once per plan.\n  let sc = cur().interior;\n  const scP = sc ? Promise.resolve(sc) : fetch(`${API}/plans/${id}/interior`, { method: \"POST\" })\n    .then((r) => (r.ok ? r.json() : null)).then((x) => { if (x) S.plans[id].interior = x; return x; }).catch(() => null);\n\n  // Rooms, floor by floor.\n  const rooms = (plan?.levels || []).flatMap((lv) => lv.rooms\n    .filter((r) => ![\"corridor\", \"staircase\", \"shaft\", \"lobby\"].includes(r.type))\n    .map((r) => ({ r, lv: lv.index })));\n  side.append(el(\"h3\", \"inx__h\", \"Rooms\"));\n  const list = el(\"ol\", \"inx__rooms\");\n  side.append(list);\n\n  const cap = el(\"p\", \"model-cap\", \"Loading the interiors…\");\n  stage.append(cap, info);\n  const { Viewer3D } = await import(\"./viewer3d.js\");\n  if (S.view !== \"interior\" || S.activeId !== id) return;\n  S.viewer?.dispose();\n  const viewer = (S.viewer = new Viewer3D(stage));\n  const pal = (S.palette ||= {});\n  const url = () => {\n    const q = new URLSearchParams();\n    if (pal.id) q.set(\"palette\", pal.id);\n    if (pal.text) q.set(\"colours\", pal.text);\n    if (pal.design) q.set(\"design\", pal.design);\n    return `${API}/plans/${id}/model.glb${q.size ? `?${q}` : \"\"}`;\n  };\n  try { await viewer.load(url()); } catch (e) { cap.textContent = `The model could not be shown (${e.message}).`; return; }\n  cap.textContent = \"Pick a room to walk into it · drag to look around\";\n\n  // Interior palettes, cycled in place.\n  let schemes = [];\n  fetch(`${API}/plans/${id}/palettes`).then((r) => r.json()).then((d) => { schemes = d.schemes || []; drawStyle(); }).catch(() => {});\n  const style = el(\"div\", \"inx__style\");\n  side.append(style);\n  const drawStyle = () => {\n    if (!schemes.length) return;\n    const i = Math.max(0, schemes.findIndex((s) => s.id === pal.id));\n    const s = schemes[i];\n    style.innerHTML = \"\";\n    style.append(el(\"span\", \"inx__k\", \"Interior style\"));\n    const row = el(\"div\", \"inx__style-row\");\n    const name = el(\"b\", null, s.name);\n    const sw = el(\"span\", \"inx__sw\");\n    for (const hex of Object.values(s.interior || {})) { const c = el(\"i\"); c.style.background = hex; sw.append(c); }\n    const nav = el(\"div\", \"inx__nav\");\n    for (const [t, step] of [[\"‹\", -1], [\"›\", 1]]) {\n      const b = el(\"button\", \"ghost-btn\", t); b.type = \"button\";\n      b.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", step < 0 ? \"Previous style\" : \"Next style\");\n      b.addEventListener(\"click\", async () => {\n        pal.id = schemes[(i + step + schemes.length) % schemes.length].id;\n        drawStyle();\n        await viewer.load(url(), { keepView: true });\n        if (current) viewer.focusRoom(current.box, current.lv, true);\n      });\n      nav.append(b);\n    }\n    row.append(name, nav);\n    style.append(row, sw, el(\"p\", \"inx__story\", s.story || \"\"));\n  };\n\n  // Walk into a room: the floors above lift away, the camera stands in a\n  // corner at eye height, and the furniture and its cost come up beside it.\n  let current = null;\n  const open = async (item, li) => {\n    list.querySelectorAll(\"li\").forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle(\"is-on\", x === li));\n    const xs = item.r.polygon.map((q) => q.x), ys = item.r.polygon.map((q) => q.y);\n    const box = { x0: Math.min(...xs), x1: Math.max(...xs), y0: Math.min(...ys), y1: Math.max(...ys) };\n    current = { box, lv: item.lv };\n    viewer.focusRoom(box, item.lv);\n    const s = await scP;\n    const rs = s?.rooms?.find((x) => x.room_id === item.r.id);\n    info.innerHTML = \"\";\n    info.append(el(\"b\", \"inx__room\", item.r.name || item.r.type));\n    info.append(el(\"span\", \"inx__meta\", `${(item.r.area ?? 0).toFixed?.(1) ?? \"\"} m² · ${floorName(item.lv)}${rs?.direction ? ` · ${rs.direction}` : \"\"}`));\n    if (rs?.furniture?.length) {\n      const ul = el(\"ul\", \"inx__items\");\n      let total = 0;\n      for (const f of rs.furniture) {\n        total += f.cost || 0;\n        const li2 = el(\"li\");\n        li2.append(el(\"span\", null, f.name), el(\"span\", \"n\", inr(f.cost || 0)));\n        ul.append(li2);\n      }\n      info.append(ul, el(\"p\", \"inx__total\", `Furniture ${inr(total)}`));\n    } else {\n      info.append(el(\"p\", \"inx__meta\", \"No loose furniture - finishes only.\"));\n    }\n    if (rs?.lighting) info.append(el(\"p\", \"inx__meta\", `${rs.lighting.target_lux} lux · ${rs.lighting.colour_temperature_k} K · ${rs.lighting.downlight_count} downlights`));\n    info.hidden = false;\n  };\n  for (const item of rooms) {\n    const li = el(\"li\");\n    const b = el(\"button\", \"inx__room-btn\"); b.type = \"button\";\n    b.append(el(\"span\", null, item.r.name || item.r.type), el(\"small\", null, `${floorName(item.lv)} · ${(+item.r.area || 0).toFixed(1)} m²`));\n    b.addEventListener(\"click\", () => open(item, li));\n    li.append(b);\n    list.append(li);\n  }\n  info.hidden = true;\n  if (rooms.length) open(rooms.find((x) => x.r.type === \"living\") || rooms[0], list.querySelector(\"li\"));\n}\n","numLines":115,"startLine":1,"totalLines":115}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\..\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\scratchpad\\interior.js"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2792cd9d-f3f2-46f7-aca4-6af9bd76ebd2","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:55:37.014Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"F:\\\\Users\\\\shrey\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\\\scratchpad\\\\interior.js\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\tasync function renderInterior() {\n2\t  const p = pane(\"interior\");\n3\t  p.innerHTML = \"\";\n4\t  const id = S.activeId;\n5\t  const plan = cur().plan;\n6\t  const wrap = el(\"div\", \"inx\");\n7\t  const side = el(\"aside\", \"inx__side\");\n8\t  const stage = el(\"div\", \"inx__stage model-stage\");\n9\t  const info = el(\"div\", \"inx__info\");\n10\t  wrap.append(side, stage);\n11\t  p.append(wrap);\n12\t\n13\t  // The interior scheme (furniture, finishes, costs), solved once per plan.\n14\t  let sc = cur().interior;\n15\t  const scP = sc ? Promise.resolve(sc) : fetch(`${API}/plans/${id}/interior`, { method: \"POST\" })\n16\t    .then((r) => (r.ok ? r.json() : null)).then((x) => { if (x) S.plans[id].interior = x; return x; }).catch(() => null);\n17\t\n18\t  // Rooms, floor by floor.\n19\t  const rooms = (plan?.levels || []).flatMap((lv) => lv.rooms\n20\t    .filter((r) => ![\"corridor\", \"staircase\", \"shaft\", \"lobby\"].includes(r.type))\n21\t    .map((r) => ({ r, lv: lv.index })));\n22\t  side.append(el(\"h3\", \"inx__h\", \"Rooms\"));\n23\t  const list = el(\"ol\", \"inx__rooms\");\n24\t  side.append(list);\n25\t\n26\t  const cap = el(\"p\", \"model-cap\", \"Loading the interiors…\");\n27\t  stage.append(cap, info);\n28\t  const { Viewer3D } = await import(\"./viewer3d.js\");\n29\t  if (S.view !== \"interior\" || S.activeId !== id) return;\n30\t  S.viewer?.dispose();\n31\t  const viewer = (S.viewer = new Viewer3D(stage));\n32\t  const pal = (S.palette ||= {});\n33\t  const url = () => {\n34\t    const q = new URLSearchParams();\n35\t    if (pal.id) q.set(\"palette\", pal.id);\n36\t    if (pal.text) q.set(\"colours\", pal.text);\n37\t    if (pal.design) q.set(\"design\", pal.design);\n38\t    return `${API}/plans/${id}/model.glb${q.size ? `?${q}` : \"\"}`;\n39\t  };\n40\t  try { await viewer.load(url()); } catch (e) { cap.textContent = `The model could not be shown (${e.message}).`; return; }\n41\t  cap.textContent = \"Pick a room to walk into it · drag to look around\";\n42\t\n43\t  // Interior palettes, cycled in place.\n44\t  let schemes = [];\n45\t  fetch(`${API}/plans/${id}/palettes`).then((r) => r.json()).then((d) => { schemes = d.schemes || []; drawStyle(); }).catch(() => {});\n46\t  const style = el(\"div\", \"inx__style\");\n47\t  side.append(style);\n48\t  const drawStyle = () => {\n49\t    if (!schemes.length) return;\n50\t    const i = Math.max(0, schemes.findIndex((s) => s.id === pal.id));\n51\t    const s = schemes[i];\n52\t    style.innerHTML = \"\";\n53\t    style.append(el(\"span\", \"inx__k\", \"Interior style\"));\n54\t    const row = el(\"div\", \"inx__style-row\");\n55\t    const name = el(\"b\", null, s.name);\n56\t    const sw = el(\"span\", \"inx__sw\");\n57\t    for (const hex of Object.values(s.interior || {})) { const c = el(\"i\"); c.style.background = hex; sw.append(c); }\n58\t    const nav = el(\"div\", \"inx__nav\");\n59\t    for (const [t, step] of [[\"‹\", -1], [\"›\", 1]]) {\n60\t      const b = el(\"button\", \"ghost-btn\", t); b.type = \"button\";\n61\t      b.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", step < 0 ? \"Previous style\" : \"Next style\");\n62\t      b.addEventListener(\"click\", async () => {\n63\t        pal.id = schemes[(i + step + schemes.length) % schemes.length].id;\n64\t        drawStyle();\n65\t        await viewer.load(url(), { keepView: true });\n66\t        if (current) viewer.focusRoom(current.box, current.lv, true);\n67\t      });\n68\t      nav.append(b);\n69\t    }\n70\t    row.append(name, nav);\n71\t    style.append(row, sw, el(\"p\", \"inx__story\", s.story || \"\"));\n72\t  };\n73\t\n74\t  // Walk into a room: the floors above lift away, the camera stands in a\n75\t  // corner at eye height, and the furniture and its cost come up beside it.\n76\t  let current = null;\n77\t  const open = async (item, li) => {\n78\t    list.querySelectorAll(\"li\").forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle(\"is-on\", x === li));\n79\t    const xs = item.r.polygon.map((q) => q.x), ys = item.r.polygon.map((q) => q.y);\n80\t    const box = { x0: Math.min(...xs), x1: Math.max(...xs), y0: Math.min(...ys), y1: Math.max(...ys) };\n81\t    current = { box, lv: item.lv };\n82\t    viewer.focusRoom(box, item.lv);\n83\t    const s = await scP;\n84\t    const rs = s?.rooms?.find((x) => x.room_id === item.r.id);\n85\t    info.innerHTML = \"\";\n86\t    info.append(el(\"b\", \"inx__room\", item.r.name || item.r.type));\n87\t    info.append(el(\"span\", \"inx__meta\", `${(item.r.area ?? 0).toFixed?.(1) ?? \"\"} m² · ${floorName(item.lv)}${rs?.direction ? ` · ${rs.direction}` : \"\"}`));\n88\t    if (rs?.furniture?.length) {\n89\t      const ul = el(\"ul\", \"inx__items\");\n90\t      let total = 0;\n91\t      for (const f of rs.furniture) {\n92\t        total += f.cost || 0;\n93\t        const li2 = el(\"li\");\n94\t        li2.append(el(\"span\", null, f.name), el(\"span\", \"n\", inr(f.cost || 0)));\n95\t        ul.append(li2);\n96\t      }\n97\t      info.append(ul, el(\"p\", \"inx__total\", `Furniture ${inr(total)}`));\n98\t    } else {\n99\t      info.append(el(\"p\", \"inx__meta\", \"No loose furniture - finishes only.\"));\n100\t    }\n101\t    if (rs?.lighting) info.append(el(\"p\", \"inx__meta\", `${rs.lighting.target_lux} lux · ${rs.lighting.colour_temperature_k} K · ${rs.lighting.downlight_count} downlights`));\n102\t    info.hidden = false;\n103\t  };\n104\t  for (const item of rooms) {\n105\t    const li = el(\"li\");\n106\t    const b = el(\"button\", \"inx__room-btn\"); b.type = \"button\";\n107\t    b.append(el(\"span\", null, item.r.name || item.r.type), el(\"small\", null, `${floorName(item.lv)} · ${(+item.r.area || 0).toFixed(1)} m²`));\n108\t    b.addEventListener(\"click\", () => open(item, li));\n109\t    li.append(b);\n110\t    list.append(li);\n111\t  }\n112\t  info.hidden = true;\n113\t  if (rooms.length) open(rooms.find((x) => x.r.type === \"living\") || rooms[0], list.querySelector(\"li\"));\n114\t}\n115\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Desktop\\AI Project\\backend","sessionId":"fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e","version":"2.1.295","gitBranch":"main","slug":"fluttering-mapping-sloth"}
{"parentUuid":"2792cd9d-f3f2-46f7-aca4-6af9bd76ebd2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\scratchpad\\hero.css","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"F:\\Users\\shrey\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\scratchpad\\hero.css","content":"\n/* ═══ HOMEPAGE: hero, showcase, committee ════════════════════════════════ */\n.compose > .compose__title { position: relative; isolation: isolate; overflow: hidden; }\n.hero3d { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: -1; }\n.hero3d canvas { width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important; display: block; }\n.hero3d::after { content: \"\"; position: absolute; inset: 0; pointer-events: none;\n  background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(11,10,9,0.92) 0%, rgba(11,10,9,0.35) 34%, rgba(11,10,9,0) 55%, rgba(11,10,9,0.55) 100%); }\n.compose__title .headline { position: relative; z-index: 1; text-shadow: 0 2px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5); }\n.hero3d__cap { position: absolute; left: var(--gut); bottom: 22px; z-index: 2; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin: 0; font-size: 11px; color: var(--cream-3); letter-spacing: 0.06em; }\n.hero3d__cap i { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: #c4553f; box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(196, 85, 63, 0.6); animation: live 2s ease-out infinite; }\n.hero3d__cap b { padding-left: 10px; border-left: 1px solid var(--rule-2); font-weight: 500; color: var(--cream-2); }\n@keyframes live { 70% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 8px rgba(196, 85, 63, 0); } 100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 rgba(196, 85, 63, 0); } }\n/* The plot drawing becomes a small live card over the model. */\n.compose__title .plotfig { position: absolute; right: var(--gut); bottom: 18px; z-index: 2; width: 210px; padding: 12px; background: rgba(11, 10, 9, 0.78); border: 1px solid var(--rule-2); backdrop-filter: blur(6px); }\n.compose__title .plotfig svg { min-height: 0; height: 170px; max-height: none; }\n.compose__title .plotfig figcaption { font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .06em; }\n\n.explain { display: grid; gap: clamp(72px, 12vh, 140px); }\n.explain__h { margin-bottom: 24px; }\n.step-card, .tile, .member { border-radius: 2px; }\n\n.show__head { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: end; gap: 24px; margin-bottom: 28px; }\n.show__head .explain__h { margin: 0; }\n.show__lede { margin: 0; max-width: 46ch; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--cream-2); }\n.show__grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.15fr 1fr 0.85fr; gap: 2px; }\n.tile { position: relative; margin: 0; display: grid; grid-template-rows: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; min-height: 420px; background: #0e0d0c; border: 1px solid var(--rule); overflow: hidden; }\n.tile img { width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: contain; padding: 18px; transition: transform .8s var(--ease); }\n.tile:hover img { transform: scale(1.03); }\n.tile__live { position: relative; min-height: 300px; }\n.tile figcaption { display: grid; gap: 4px; padding: 16px 18px 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }\n.tile figcaption b { font: 600 16px var(--display); }\n.tile figcaption span { font-size: 13px; color: var(--cream-3); line-height: 1.5; }\n.facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; align-content: center; gap: 28px 18px; padding: 28px 22px; }\n.facts b { display: block; font: 500 clamp(36px, 4vw, 56px)/1 var(--display); letter-spacing: -0.02em; color: var(--cream); }\n.facts span { display: block; margin-top: 6px; font-size: 12.5px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--cream-3); }\n\n.board__grid { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(190px, 1fr)); gap: 2px; }\n.member { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 28px 1fr; grid-template-rows: auto auto; column-gap: 12px; row-gap: 2px; align-items: center; padding: 16px; background: rgba(var(--c-rgb), 0.025); border: 1px solid var(--rule); transition: background .25s var(--ease), border-color .25s var(--ease); }\n.member:hover { background: rgba(var(--c-rgb), 0.06); border-color: var(--rule-2); }\n.member__gl { grid-row: 1 / span 2; width: 22px; height: 22px; fill: none; stroke: var(--ochre); stroke-width: 1.2; }\n.member[data-pig=\"hingula\"] .member__gl { stroke: #c4553f; }\n.member[data-pig=\"indigo\"] .member__gl { stroke: #a39c92; }\n.member[data-pig=\"orpiment\"] .member__gl { stroke: #e8dcc6; }\n.member b { font: 600 13.5px var(--ui); color: var(--cream); }\n.member span { font-size: 12px; color: var(--cream-3); }\n\n.cta { display: grid; justify-items: start; gap: 22px; padding-bottom: 40px; }\n.cta__h { margin: 0; font: 500 clamp(44px, 7vw, 110px)/0.92 var(--display); letter-spacing: -0.03em; text-transform: uppercase; }\n.cta__go { height: 48px; padding: 0 24px; border-radius: 2px; }\n\n.step-card { border: 1px solid var(--rule); }\n\n@media (max-width: 1100px) { .show__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } .tile--facts { grid-column: 1 / -1; min-height: 0; } }\n@media (max-width: 900px) {\n  .compose > .compose__title { min-height: 80svh; }\n  .show__head { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n  .show__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }\n  .compose__title .plotfig { display: none; }\n}\n","numLines":60,"startLine":1,"totalLines":60}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\..\\Temp\\claude\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\scratchpad\\hero.css"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"dc22d6a0-1b6b-4b39-9b79-35a71fb62620","timestamp":"2026-10-11T05:55:37.014Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"F:\\\\Users\\\\shrey\\\\Temp\\\\claude\\\\F--Users-shrey-Desktop-AI-Project\\\\fd077be5-cd09-4d91-beb4-30df27c1398e\\\\scratchpad\\\\hero.css\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\n2\t/* ═══ HOMEPAGE: hero, showcase, committee ═══════════